 behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene, so no tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows; docs that disagree with code. Never read or print holdout prompt text (split holdout in command-prompts.jsonl, or holdout-prompts.jsonl): counts only. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder. Run tests as env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file> from .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime, single files only.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/5227d078-62ce-41ed-b96c-d1d6535a01ff/scratchpad/review-instructions-2.txt, lines 1-1\n1: Code review of command surfacing, PASS TWO. Scope: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/5227d078-62ce-41ed-b96c-d1d6535a01ff/scratchpad/review-scope-2.txt lists the files, one per line as area TAB path TAB changed-since-pass-one. Review the files whose area equals your lineage label without its -2 suffix (the label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir), plus shared docs that describe them. PASS ONE is closed: its 43 findings, their verdicts and their fixes are in specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md (section 3.1 is the table, section 8 the deferred items). Read that table for your area first. Your work, in this order: (1) for each pass-one finding in your area, re-read the code and say whether the fix holds; report a fix that does not hold as a finding that names the old id. (2) Review every file marked yes (changed since pass one) line by line for a defect the fix introduced. (3) Then look for new defects in the rest of your area. Do NOT re-report a pass-one finding whose fix holds, a deferred item from section 8, R4-P2-003 (an AGENTS.md edit that waits on the operator) or the refuted finding. Every finding is P0, P1 or P2 with file:line and a concrete input that shows it. Check: behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene, so no tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows; docs that disagree with code. Never read or print holdout prompt text (split holdout in command-prompts.jsonl, or holdout-prompts.jsonl): counts only. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder. Run tests as env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run <file> from .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime, single files only."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/5227d078-62ce-41ed-b96c-d1d6535a01ff/scratchpad/review-instructions-2.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570146053,"end":1794570147070}}}}
