{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570220182,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b8713c001V7T39muME4ClHZ","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","messageID":"msg_1d4b85b61001eyogjsd4QEfMU0","type":"tool","id":"call_be3daa4c4ba546bcbf4f6f98","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-252\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner Lineage\n2: \n3: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n4: \n5: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder target)\n6: - Fan-out lineage: `accuracy-runner` (artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner`)\n7: - Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n8: - Stop conditions: legal convergence at `convergenceThreshold=0.10`, or `maxIterations=5`, whichever comes first\n9: - Success criteria: every accuracy-runner scoped file reviewed at least once; findings carry `file:line`; holdout hygiene verified by counts only\n10: - Review focus (operator bound): command-surfacing review of routing-accuracy runners and their corpora; cross-runtime behaviour (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh); safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene; docs that disagree with code\n11: - Resource map: `resource-map.md` not present; skipping coverage gate\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## 2. TOPIC\n16: \n17: Command surfacing behavior for the routed skill/command advisor, restricted to the `accuracy-runner` area: the routing-accuracy measurement harness (`runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/`), prompt corpora and fixtures, cost-measurement benches, transcript scoring, transcript/offer tests, and the legacy fidelity tests plus the manual-testing playbook that documents how to run them.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n22: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n23: [All dimensions complete]\n24: \n25: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n26: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n27: \n28: - Not reviewing `scorer-attach`, `render-hooks-plugin`, or `doctor-install` area files except as read-only context when a cross-area contract is required\n29: - Not reviewing the spec packet docs as an authorship target; they are traceability context\n30: - Not fixing anything: the review is observation-only\n31: - Not reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout coverage is counts-only\n32: \n33: ---\n34: \n35: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n36: \n37: - Legal convergence (all dimensions covered plus stabilization) at or below `convergenceThreshold`\n38: - `maxIterations=5` reached (`stopReason: maxIterationsReached`)\n39: - Any active P0 blocks a PASS verdict but does not stop iteration dispatch by itself; the P0 override keeps `newFindingsRatio >= 0.50`\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n44: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n45: - [x] correctness\n46: - [x] security\n47: - [x] traceability\n48: - [x] maintainability\n49: \n50: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n51: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n52: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n53: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n54: - P1 (Required): 0\n55: - P2 (Suggestions): 9\n56: - Resolved: 4\n57: \n58: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n59: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n60: - Reading the invariant at both ends (holdout guard in scorer/runner vs. report publication in baseline) surfaced a leak a single-file read would miss (iteration 1).\n61: - Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\n62: - Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\n63: - Building a per-runtime permission matrix from the six `buildArgv` entries turned \"the arena contains it\" into a checkable claim and exposed which runtimes have no OS-level bound (iteration 2).\n64: - Comparing the header threat model against `childEnv` caught an overclaim that no single function read would show (iteration 2).\n65: - Re-deriving every numeric floor in `spec.md` from the committed baseline turned traceability into arithmetic instead of a prose comparison, and all four held (iteration 3).\n66: - Checking a playbook's failure-triage symbols against the tree proved that chapter executable rather than assuming it (iteration 3).\n67: - Reading the independent-holdout gate as doctrine, not just as another test, produced the evidence that reclassified a P1 honestly instead of carrying an overstated claim to synthesis (iteration 4).\n68: - Checking how a bench is included (vitest env switch plus tsconfig exclusion) explained why a seven-runtime matrix with two keys survives CI (iteration 4).\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n73: - An early suspicion that the README named a non-existent Python file was wrong; the file exists, so the finding was narrowed to the real inventory drift (iteration 1).\n74: - Trying to promote the \"no arena assertion\" gap to P1 failed the reach test: the documented operator path runs from the arena clone, whose empty remote list satisfies the guard, so it stays P2 hardening (iteration 2).\n75: - A first reading of the runner README's restore sentence looked like a code defect; the code path is deliberate (exit 3, no restore), so the finding was narrowed to the documentation gap (iteration 3).\n76: - A bench typed against the full runtime tuple silently fails for five runtimes because both the type-check and the test glob exclude it by default (iteration 4).\n77: - Re-adjudicating two P1 findings to P2 after reading the independent-holdout gate's own doctrine and the runner's enume