` as a standalone finding: required to observe an ask row and covered by the arena model; folded into the environment finding (iteration 2, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:176-178`).\n183: - Prompt leakage through argv: corpus prompts are not secret and holdout ids are refused before a prompt reaches argv (iteration 2, evidence: `run-command-behaviour.mjs:583-594,724-727`).\n184: - NC-011 stale failure triage: ruled out; `MODE_COMMANDS`, `DEPTH_WORDING` and the `command-speckit-save` owner row exist at the cited locations (iteration 3, evidence: `command-attach.ts:15,306`, `projection.ts:893-900`).\n185: - Packet floor misstatement: ruled out; typed 44/44, plain tune 23/45, false offers 0/35 and holdout 1/44 all meet the recorded floors (iteration 3, evidence: `command-routing-baseline.json`).\n186: \n187: ---\n188: \n189: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n190: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n191: - Dimension: none - Focus area: none; the loop stops at `maxIterations=5` without legal convergence. - Reason: `maxIterations` cap reached; synthesis follows. - Rotation status: D1-D4 complete plus stabilization pass. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: blocked (no live execution evidence for the cross-runtime proof); productive (holdout doctrine and severity re-adjudication). - Required evidence: none for iteration dispatch; synthesis reads the registry and iteration files. Review verdict: PASS\n192: \n193: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n194: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n195: \n196: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n197: \n198: - Target pointers: 29 `accuracy-runner` files from `review-scope.txt` (routing-accuracy runners/corpora, cost benches, transcript/offer tests, legacy fidelity tests, manual-testing playbook). Shared docs: `system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md`, `README.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `runtime/scripts/README.md`, `runtime/tests/README.md`, `feature-catalog/*`, `sk-doc` docs.\n199: - Behavior claims to verify: routed command surfacing must be cross-runtime correct (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh); a mutating command must never be offered unsafely (no implicit `:auto` invocation of a writing workflow); holdout rows must never be read by tune/fix/report paths; documentation must match runner behavior.\n200: - Reuse and conventions: append-gateway state recording, `validate.sh --strict` evidence discipline, P0/P1/P2 severity ladder, three-artifact iteration contract.\n201: - Review risks and gaps: holdout prompt text is out of read scope (counts only); fan-out containment forbids running repo tooling that writes outside the lineage, so runners are audited by reading, not by execution; coverage graph seed skipped by containment (see edge cases).\n202: \n203: ---\n204: \n205: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n206: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n207: \n208: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n209: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n210: | `spec_code` | core | pass | 3 | All four numeric floors re-derived from the committed baseline: typed 44/44, plain tune 23/45, false offers 0/35, holdout 1/44. |\n211: | `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | 3 | Parent packet has no checklist; owning phase 007 closing tasks remain open. |\n212: | `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | 3 | No agent definition owns the accuracy-runner area. |\n213: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | 2 | Six runtime argv tables read; three bypass approvals; end-to-end proof still open in phase 007. |\n214: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | 3 | `--real-embedding` refuses `--write` as documented. |\n215: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | pass | 3 | NC-011 executable as written; all triage symbols resolve. |\n216: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n217: \n218: ---\n219: \n220: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n221: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n222: \n223: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n224: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n225: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/` (12 files) | D1, D2 | 2 | 1 P1, 2 P2 | partial |\n226: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs`, `measure-embedder-cost.mjs` | D1, D2 | 2 | 0 | partial |\n227: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts` | - | - | - | pending |\n228: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/fixtures/gate2-golden-prompts.jsonl`, `skill-advisor-regression-cases.jsonl` | - | - | - | pending |\n229: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-offer.vitest.ts`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` | D1 (slice) | 1 | 1 P1 | partial |\n230: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/legacy/` (5 files) | - | - | - | pending |\n231: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`, `native-cli-tools/hub-command-attachment.md` | D3 | 3 | 0 | partial (chapter verified, root playbook pending maintainability pass) |\n232: \n233: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n234: \n235: ---\n236: \n237: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n238: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n239: - Max iterations: 5\n240: - Convergence threshold: 0.10\n241: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n242: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n243: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n244: - Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-accuracy-runner-1794550137809-1ecgc7, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n245: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n246: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n247: - Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n248: - Severity threshold: P2\n249: - Review target type: spec-folder\n250: - Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n251: - Started: 2026-11-13T06:12:20Z\n252: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-252\n1: # Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner Lineage\n2: \n3: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n4: \n5: - Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder target)\n6: - Fan-out lineage: `accuracy-runner` (artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner`)\n7: - Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n8: - Stop conditions: legal convergence at `convergenceThreshold=0.10`, or `maxIterations=5`, whichever comes first\n9: - Success criteria: every accuracy-runner scoped file reviewed at least once; findings carry `file:line`; holdout hygiene verified by counts only\n10: - Review focus (operator bound): command-surfacing review of routing-accuracy runners and their corpora; cross-runtime behaviour (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh); safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene; docs that disagree with code\n11: - Resource map: `resource-map.md` not present; skipping coverage gate\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## 2. TOPIC\n16: \n17: Command surfacing behavior for the routed skill/command advisor, restricted to the `accuracy-runner` area: the routing-accuracy measurement harness (`runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/`), prompt corpora and fixtures, cost-measurement benches, transcript scoring, transcript/offer tests, and the legacy fidelity tests plus the manual-testing playbook that documents how to run them.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n22: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n23: [All dimensions complete]\n24: \n25: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n26: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n27: \n28: - Not reviewing `scorer-attach`, `render-hooks-plugin`, or `doctor-install` area files except as read-only context when a cross-area contract is required\n29: - Not reviewing the spec packet docs as an authorship target; they are traceability context\n30: - Not fixing anything: the review is observation-only\n31: - Not reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout coverage is counts-only\n32: \n33: ---\n34: \n35: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n36: \n37: - Legal convergence (all dimensions covered plus stabilization) at or below `convergenceThreshold`\n38: - `maxIterations=5` reached (`stopReason: maxIterationsReached`)\n39: - Any active P0 blocks a PASS verdict but does not stop iteration dispatch by itself; the P0 override keeps `newFindingsRatio >= 0.50`\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n44: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n45: - [x] correctness\n46: - [x] security\n47: - [x] traceability\n48: - [x] maintainability\n49: \n50: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n51: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n52: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n53: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n54: - P1 (Required): 0\n55: - P2 (Suggestions): 9\n56: - Resolved: 4\n57: \n58: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n59: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n60: - Reading the invariant at both ends (holdout guard in scorer/runner vs. report publication in baseline) surfaced a leak a single-file read would miss (iteration 1).\n61: - Counting corpus splits through `split`/`row_type` tallies instead of prompt text kept the review holdout-safe while still proving composition (iteration 1).\n62: - Checking every renderer head shape against `BRIEF_PATTERN` eliminated a suspected false-negative instead of reporting it (iteration 1).\n63: - Building a per-runtime permission matrix from the six `buildArgv` entries turned \"the arena contains it\" into a checkable claim and exposed which runtimes have no OS-level bound (iteration 2).\n64: - Comparing the header threat model against `childEnv` caught an overclaim that no single function read would show (iteration 2).\n65: - Re-deriving every numeric floor in `spec.md` from the committed baseline turned traceability into arithmetic instead of a prose comparison, and all four held (iteration 3).\n66: - Checking a playbook's failure-triage symbols against the tree proved that chapter executable rather than assuming it (iteration 3).\n67: - Reading the independent-holdout gate as doctrine, not just as another test, produced the evidence that reclassified a P1 honestly instead of carrying an overstated claim to synthesis (iteration 4).\n68: - Checking how a bench is included (vitest env switch plus tsconfig exclusion) explained why a seven-runtime matrix with two keys survives CI (iteration 4).\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n73: - An early suspicion that the README named a non-existent Python file was wrong; the file exists, so the finding was narrowed to the real inventory drift (iteration 1).\n74: - Trying to promote the \"no arena assertion\" gap to P1 failed the reach test: the documented operator path runs from the arena clone, whose empty remote list satisfies the guard, so it stays P2 hardening (iteration 2).\n75: - A first reading of the runner README's restore sentence looked like a code defect; the code path is deliberate (exit 3, no restore), so the finding was narrowed to the documentation gap (iteration 3).\n76: - A bench typed against the full runtime tuple silently fails for five runtimes because both the type-check and the test glob exclude it by default (iteration 4).\n77: - Re-adjudicating two P1 findings to P2 after reading the independent-holdout gate's own doctrine and the runner's enumerated network claim (iteration 4); both stay active so the merge still sees them.\n78: \n79: ---\n80: \n81: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n82: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n83: ### `--auto` on OpenCode as an unconditional finding: the arena plus the no-remote guard is the documented containment model, and auto-approval is required to observe an ask row at all (`:176-178`). Folded into finding 1 as a contributing runtime, not reported separately. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n84: - What was tried: `--auto` on OpenCode as an unconditional finding: the arena plus the no-remote guard is the documented containment model, and auto-approval is required to observe an ask row at all (`:176-178`). Folded into finding 1 as a contributing runtime, not reported separately.\n85: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n86: - Do NOT retry: `--auto` on OpenCode as an unconditional finding: the arena plus the no-remote guard is the documented containment model, and auto-approval is required to observe an ask row at all (`:176-178`). Folded into finding 1 as a contributing runtime, not reported separately.\n87: \n88: ### `--dry-run` is not side-effect free: it still replays the Claude hook (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`), which spawns a process. Ruled out as a finding because the code comments state the replay explicitly and no documentation claims a dry run spawns nothing; recorded as a behavior note only. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n89: - What was tried: `--dry-run` is not side-effect free: it still replays the Claude hook (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`), which spawns a process. Ruled out as a finding because the code comments state the replay explicitly and no documentation claims a dry run spawns nothing; recorded as a behavior note only.\n90: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n91: - Do NOT retry: `--dry-run` is not side-effect free: it still replays the Claude hook (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:1043-1047`), which spawns a process. Ruled out as a finding because the code comments state the replay explicitly and no documentation claims a dry run spawns nothing; recorded as a behavior note only.\n92: \n93: ### `console.log` in the bench: it mirrors the documented bench log shape (`:109-110`) and creates no defect. -- BLOCKED (iteration 4, 1 attempts)\n94: - What was tried: 