{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570302042,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b9acef0016NWkR45S0Tr2Dy","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","messageID":"msg_1d4b98c7d001FGOfw3gOBc3aPT","type":"tool","id":"call_7b6bca0d8e6841c589c93db4","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research; git show b3b5ae8314 --stat | head -40; echo \"=== my area diff in b3b5 ===\"; git show b3b5ae8314 -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts | head -400"},"output":"commit b3b5ae83146dd0f7197f4256a3231f429ee5a2f9\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 10:53:18 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(system-skill-advisor): close review pass one across the command surfacing code\n    \n    Review pass one confirmed 43 advisory findings in 13 work groups. This\n    change fixes them with a test for each fix where one can exist.\n    \n    The AGENTS.md embed now undoes a write that fails after its backup and\n    exits 3, checks every backup entry before it restores any, fails on a\n    foreign line as on a dropped one and refuses a linked router or Cursor\n    mirror it would write through. A second fault during the restore still\n    prints the backup and undo lines.\n    \n    A hub command is no longer offered on a no-edit prompt, a deep-loop\n    command only when the prompt types that command or asks for depth, and a\n    file name such as /create:skill.md no longer reads as a typed command.\n    The dead COMMAND_POLICIES table is gone at its emitter. The renderer\n    prints (needs a mode) with the owner skill on any row and takes the\n    child downgrade's class from the command it prints.\n    \n    The behaviour runner gives a live turn an allowlisted environment and\n    refuses a checkout the arena builder did not mark. The routing baseline\n    publishes no per-row outcome for a holdout row. The advisor subprocess\n    caps its child's output, the session readers open the path their\n    containment check resolved, and a hook counts as wired only when a\n    command runs it.\n    \n    Floors held: typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35, scorer eval\n    [160,50,21,5]. Suite: 182 files, 1,744 passed. Doctor tests 1,188 and\n    reader tests 93, 0 failed.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation\n    Commit-Id: 0013831\n\n .../doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml      |   5 +-\n .../assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt       |   2 +-\n .../doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt  |   4 +-\n .../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml     |   2 +-\n=== my area diff in b3b5 ===\ncommit b3b5ae83146dd0f7197f4256a3231f429ee5a2f9\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 10:53:18 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(system-skill-advisor): close review pass one across the command surfacing code\n    \n    Review pass one confirmed 43 advisory findings in 13 work groups. This\n    change fixes them with a test for each fix where one can exist.\n    \n    The AGENTS.md embed now undoes a write that fails after its backup and\n    exits 3, checks every backup entry before it restores any, fails on a\n    foreign line as on a dropped one and refuses a linked router or Cursor\n    mirror it would write through. A second fault during the restore still\n    prints the backup and undo lines.\n    \n    A hub command is no longer offered on a no-edit prompt, a deep-loop\n    command only when the prompt types that command or asks for depth, and a\n    file name such as /create:skill.md no longer reads as a typed command.\n    The dead COMMAND_POLICIES table is gone at its emitter. The renderer\n    prints (needs a mode) with the owner skill on any row and takes the\n    child downgrade's class from the command it prints.\n    \n    The behaviour runner gives a live turn an allowlisted environment and\n    refuses a checkout the arena builder did not mark. The routing baseline\n    publishes no per-row outcome for a holdout row. The advisor subprocess\n    caps its child's output, the session readers open the path their\n    containment check resolved, and a hook counts as wired only when a\n    command runs it.\n    \n    Floors held: typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35, scorer eval\n    [160,50,21,5]. Suite: 182 files, 1,744 passed. Doctor tests 1,188 and\n    reader tests 93, 0 failed.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation\n    Commit-Id: 0013831\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\nindex dad2d44b04..ceddc92c21 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n // MODULE: Hook Brief Signal/Noise Bench\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n-// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime (claude/opencode),\n+// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime (the iteration measured Claude and OpenCode, and the rest read not-recorded),\n // loads the iter-4 7-axis adapter divergence matrix as a fixture, and\n // asserts non-zero signal counts per runtime. Collector-shape coverage for\n // spec_kit.advisor.recommendation_emitted_total is kept separate from the\n@@ -24,8 +24,14 @@ const F22_AXES = [\n ] as const;\n \n const SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX: Record<typeof ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES[number], Record<typeof F22_AXES[number], string>> = {\n-  claude:  { inputFieldNames: 'prompt-only', cwdResolution: 'input-or-process', inputSource: 'stdin-only', outputShape: 'hookSpecificOutput', timeoutHandling: 'none', renderThresholdOverride: 'none', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'none' },\n-  opencode:   { inputFieldNames: '3-fallbacks', cwdResolution: 'input-or-request-or-process', inputSource: 'stdin-or-argv', outputShape: 'hookSpecificOutput', timeoutHandling: 'env-3000ms', renderThresholdOverride: 'forced-0.8/0.35', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'none' },\n+  claude:   { inputFieldNames: 'prompt-only', cwdResolution: 'input-or-process', inputSource: 'stdin-only', outputShape: 'hookSpecificOutput', timeoutHandling: 'none', renderThresholdOverride: 'none', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'none' },\n+  opencode: { inputFieldNames: '3-fallbacks', cwdResolution: 'input-or-request-or-process', inputSource: 'stdin-or-argv', outputShape: 'hookSpecificOutput', timeoutHandling: 'env-3000ms', renderThresholdOverride: 'forced-0.8/0.35', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'none' },\n+  // An invented axis reading would pass for a measured one, so a runtime nobody probed reads not-recorded.\n+  pi:       { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n+  codex:    { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n+  cursor:   { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n+  devin:    { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n+  dsh:      { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n };\n \n function buildRecommendations(runtime: string): readonly AdvisorRecommendation[] {\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\nindex e8ea3e9d10..c98db0579c 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ Use this file to identify the folder boundary, the likely verification path and\n \n | Metric | Value |\n |---|---:|\n-| Code files | 9 |\n+| Code files | 14 |\n | README scope | Direct files in this folder |\n | Audit context | Internal validation notes |\n \n@@ -107,11 +107,24 @@ A typed command travels on its owner. It is delivered only when the leading reco\n | `gate3-corpus-runner.mjs` | MJS source file in this folder. |\n | `score-routing-corpus.py` | PY source file in this folder. |\n | `command-prompts.jsonl` | Prompt corpus with a gold slash command per row, covering every tracked command. |\n-| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. |\n-| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers on a turn whose brief arrived, `deliveryUnknown` counts rows whose brief state is `unknown`, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n+| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. |\n+| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts rows whose brief state is `unknown`, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n | `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input. |\n-| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n+| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n | `command-routing-baseline.json` | Captured command routing numbers that `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` holds the scorer to. |\n+| `build-holdout.mjs` | Builds the frozen holdout from three separately authored fixtures that are disjoint from the labeled corpus, copying each row's own label and keeping its provenance in `source_type` and `origin_fixture`. Family-normalized dedup keeps the first occurrence and drops any prompt that collides with the training corpus. `--write` rewrites `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. |\n+| `capture-local-native-divergence-ledger.mjs` | Recomputes the strict Python/native top-1 divergence set the ratchet replays. An existing approval is kept only while its prompt hash and both current tops still match, so the output is a capture of live scoring rather than a hand-edited fixture. Scores both scorers against a skill graph indexed fresh into a temporary directory with the clock pinned to the capture day, and `--write` records the result. |\n+| `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` | Captures scorer accuracy across the full corpus, the independent holdout, the frozen ambiguity slice and the named intent buckets under the reproducible filesystem projection, then `--write` records `scorer-eval-baseline.json`. Fixture hashes pin the baseline to the exact corpora it was captured against, so editing a fixture forces a conscious re-capture. `--misses` prints one failing prompt per line. |\n+| `derive-ambiguity-slice.mjs` | Derives the frozen ambiguity slice as the corpus rows whose top-2 fused-score margin is at or below `tau`, keeping each row's existing gold label, so a regression that only hurts contested prompts still fails a gate. `--write` rewrites `ambiguity-prompts.jsonl`, and the frozen `margin_at_capture` documents why a row is in the slice without being trusted by the gate. |\n+| `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` | Builds the arena a live arm runs in: a clone of the branch tip with no remote and no outer repository, plus the ignored build trees copied in and stamped at copy time so the freshness guard reads them as fresh. It refuses a destination inside a repository or one that already exists, and skips every file whose name begins with `.env` so no secret follows the build output in. |\n+| `reject-unknown-options.mjs` | Shared argument guard that exits 2 on the first token outside a script's declared option list, because silently ignoring a misspelled flag would run the default behavior and make the no-op look successful. |\n+| `score-outcome-rerank.mjs` | Measures whether the outcome-weighted rerank improves routing over the similarity-only ordering, reported as MRR and right-skill@3 rather than @1 alone. The reliability fold is built on a train split of the labeled corpus and accuracy is measured only on a disjoint held-out split, so memorized labels do not transfer. Read-only against the skill graph. |\n+| `worktree-restore.mjs` | Restores one measured turn's checkout to the snapshot taken before it, leaving a path that was already dirty alone and dropping a staged path HEAD does not know. A second snapshot after the restore reports what still differs, so the caller fails the run instead of claiming a clean worktree. |\n+| `ambiguity-prompts.jsonl` | Frozen ambiguity slice written by `derive-ambiguity-slice.mjs` and read by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`. Each row carries `id`, `prompt`, `skill_top_1`, `bucket`, `source_type`, `tau`, `margin_at_capture` and `captured_at`. |\n+| `doctor-prompts.jsonl` | Doctor routing slice read by `tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts`. Each row carries `id`, `prompt`, `expected_top`, `expected_second` and `wave`, where a wave scores only after every doctor bridge its rows expect is active, so a half-shipped bridge cannot fail the gate. |\n+| `holdout-prompts.jsonl` | Frozen holdout written by `build-holdout.mjs` from three separately authored fixtures disjoint from the labeled corpus, and read by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` as its unseen split. |\n+| `labeled-prompts.jsonl` | Labeled training corpus with `id`, `prompt`, `skill_top_1`, `skill_correct`, `bucket`, `source_type`, `notes`, `gate3_triggers` and `gate3_reason_category`. Scored by `score-routing-corpus.py`, `score-outcome-rerank.mjs` and `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`, and read by the divergence ledger, the ambiguity deriver, the holdout builder and the gate 3 corpus runner. |\n+| `scorer-eval-baseline.json` | Scorer eval baseline written by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`: `schemaVersion`, `capturedAt`, `capturedAtSha`, `env`, the fixture hashes and `metrics` for the full corpus, holdout, ambiguity slice, gold-none false fire, intent buckets and unknown count. The ratchet gate re-scores live under the same environment and holds every metric to it. |\n \n ---\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\nindex 9ed377507f..aba01f7013 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\n@@ -492,6 +492,9 @@ export async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n       // command, which the behaviour run line records as `offeredCommand`.\n       const offered = landed.some((command) => command !== null);\n       const isPlainSplit = row.row_type === 'plain' && (row.split === 'tune' || row.split === 'holdout');\n+      // A holdout row's outcome is what the split exists to keep unseen, so\n+      // only its counts are published.\n+      const publishRow = row.split !== 'holdout';\n \n       // A hub can name the slash command its route would take, which is reach a\n       // reader otherwise gets only by translating the workflow mode by hand.\n@@ -509,13 +512,15 @@ export async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n       if (row.row_type === 'typed') {\n         addRow(typed, top1Hit, top3Hit);\n         addAttachedRow(typedAttached, top1Hit, deliveredHit);\n-        typedRowResults[row.id] = {\n-          expected_command: expected,\n-          top: ids[0] ?? null,\n-          carried: top1Hit ? 'own' : deliveredHit ? 'attached' : null,\n-          command: delivered ?? null,\n-          policy: deliveredPolicy,\n-        };\n+        if (publishRow) {\n+          typedRowResults[row.id] = {\n+            expected_command: expected,\n+            top: ids[0] ?? null,\n+            carried: top1Hit ? 'own' : deliveredHit ? 'attached' : null,\n+            command: delivered ?? null,\n+            policy: deliveredPolicy,\n+          };\n+        }\n       }\n       if (isPlainSplit) {\n         addRow(plain[row.split], top1Hit, top3Hit);\n@@ -523,7 +528,7 @@ export async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n         const family = attachedFamilyTally(plainAttachedByFamily, expected);\n         if (family) addAttachedRow(family[row.split], top1Hit, attachedHit);\n       }\n-      if (attached !== undefined) attachedRows[row.id] = attached;\n+      if (publishRow && attached !== undefined) attachedRows[row.id] = attached;\n       if (row.row_type === 'typed' && result?.ambiguous === true && isBridgeOwnerPair(idToCommand, ids, expected)) {\n         sameOwnerAmbiguous.push(row.id);\n       }\n@@ -534,7 +539,9 @@ export async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n         else if (isPlainSplit) addRow(commandTally.plain[row.split], top1Hit, top3Hit);\n       }\n \n-      rows[row.id] = { expected_command: expected, top: ids[0] ?? null, top1: top1Hit, top3: top3Hit, offered };\n+      if (publishRow) {\n+        rows[row.id] = { expected_command: expected, top: ids[0] ?? null, top1: top1Hit, top3: top3Hit, offered };\n+      }\n \n       const isSlashVariant = row.row_type === 'slash-variant';\n       // Silence is the requirement for a near miss, a prompt that must not\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\nindex 1c9fb9885f..eec4bce796 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {\n   \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n   \"capturedAt\": \"2026-10-11\",\n-  \"capturedAtSha\": \"99b68d8b3d\",\n+  \"capturedAtSha\": \"320e7b64d4\",\n   \"corpusSha256\": \"sha256:698da57b02159a756dbba5d6a2c9a3c6d14588d07e96be268567835cf36448b8\",\n   \"bridgeCounts\": {\n     \"commandMetadata\": 27,\n@@ -933,13 +933,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-agent-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:agent\",\n-      \"top\": \"sk-code\",\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-benchmark-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:benchmark\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -954,13 +947,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-benchmark-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:benchmark\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-changelog-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:changelog\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -975,13 +961,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-changelog-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:changelog\",\n-      \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-command-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:command\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -996,13 +975,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-command-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:command\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-diff-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:diff\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -1017,13 +989,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-diff-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:diff\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-feature-catalog-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:feature-catalog\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -1038,13 +1003,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-feature-catalog-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:feature-catalog\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-goal-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:goal\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -1059,13 +1017,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-goal-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:goal\",\n-      \"top\": \"system-spec-kit\",\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-manual-testing-playbook-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:manual-testing-playbook\",\n       \"top\": \"create:manual-testing-playbook\",\n@@ -1080,13 +1031,6 @@\n       \"top3\": true,\n       \"offered\": true\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-manual-testing-playbook-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:manual-testing-playbook\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-readme-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:readme\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -1101,13 +1045,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-readme-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:readme\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-repo-rule-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:repo-rule\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -1122,13 +1059,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-repo-rule-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:repo-rule\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-skill-parent-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -1143,13 +1073,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-skill-parent-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:skill-parent\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-skill-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:skill\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -1164,13 +1087,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-skill-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:skill\",\n-      \"top\": \"cli-external-orchestration\",\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-with-human-voice-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:with-human-voice\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -1185,13 +1101,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-with-human-voice-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:with-human-voice\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-doctor-agents-md-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/doctor:agents-md\",\n       \"top\": \"command-doctor-agents-md-check\",\n@@ -1206,13 +1115,6 @@\n       \"top3\": true,\n       \"offered\": true\n     },\n-    \"cmd-doctor-agents-md-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/doctor:agents-md\",\n-      \"top\": \"command-doctor-agents-md-check\",\n-      \"top1\": true,\n-      \"top3\": true,\n-      \"offered\": true\n-    },\n     \"cmd-doctor-ci-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/doctor:ci\",\n       \"top\": \"command-doctor-ci-report\",\n@@ -1227,13 +1129,6 @@\n       \"top3\": true,\n       \"offered\": true\n     },\n-    \"cmd-doctor-ci-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/doctor:ci\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-doctor-deep-loop-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/doctor:deep-loop\",\n       \"top\": \"command-doctor-deep-loop\",\n@@ -1248,13 +1143,6 @@\n       \"top3\": true,\n       \"offered\": true\n     },\n-    \"cmd-doctor-deep-loop-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/doctor:deep-loop\",\n-      \"top\": \"system-deep-loop\",\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-doctor-env-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/doctor:env\",\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"commit b3b5ae83146dd0f7197f4256a3231f429ee5a2f9\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 10:53:18 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(system-skill-advisor): close review pass one across the command surfacing code\n    \n    Review pass one confirmed 43 advisory findings in 13 work groups. This\n    change fixes them with a test for each fix where one can exist.\n    \n    The AGENTS.md embed now undoes a write that fails after its backup and\n    exits 3, checks every backup entry before it restores any, fails on a\n    foreign line as on a dropped one and refuses a linked router or Cursor\n    mirror it would write through. A second fault during the restore still\n    prints the backup and undo lines.\n    \n    A hub command is no longer offered on a no-edit prompt, a deep-loop\n    command only when the prompt types that command or asks for depth, and a\n    file name such as /create:skill.md no longer reads as a typed command.\n    The dead COMMAND_POLICIES table is gone at its emitter. The renderer\n    prints (needs a mode) with the owner skill on any row and takes the\n    child downgrade's class from the command it prints.\n    \n    The behaviour runner gives a live turn an allowlisted environment and\n    refuses a checkout the arena builder did not mark. The routing baseline\n    publishes no per-row outcome for a holdout row. The advisor subprocess\n    caps its child's output, the session readers open the path their\n    containment check resolved, and a hook counts as wired only when a\n    command runs it.\n    \n    Floors held: typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35, scorer eval\n    [160,50,21,5]. Suite: 182 files, 1,744 passed. Doctor tests 1,188 and\n    reader tests 93, 0 failed.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation\n    Commit-Id: 0013831\n\n .../doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml      |   5 +-\n .../assets/doctor-agents-md-presentation.txt       |   2 +-\n .../doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt  |   4 +-\n .../commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install.yaml     |   2 +-\n=== my area diff in b3b5 ===\ncommit b3b5ae83146dd0f7197f4256a3231f429ee5a2f9\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 10:53:18 2026 +0100\n\n    fix(system-skill-advisor): close review pass one across the command surfacing code\n    \n    Review pass one confirmed 43 advisory findings in 13 work groups. This\n    change fixes them with a test for each fix where one can exist.\n    \n    The AGENTS.md embed now undoes a write that fails after its backup and\n    exits 3, checks every backup entry before it restores any, fails on a\n    foreign line as on a dropped one and refuses a linked router or Cursor\n    mirror it would write through. A second fault during the restore still\n    prints the backup and undo lines.\n    \n    A hub command is no longer offered on a no-edit prompt, a deep-loop\n    command only when the prompt types that command or asks for depth, and a\n    file name such as /create:skill.md no longer reads as a typed command.\n    The dead COMMAND_POLICIES table is gone at its emitter. The renderer\n    prints (needs a mode) with the owner skill on any row and takes the\n    child downgrade's class from the command it prints.\n    \n    The behaviour runner gives a live turn an allowlisted environment and\n    refuses a checkout the arena builder did not mark. The routing baseline\n    publishes no per-row outcome for a holdout row. The advisor subprocess\n    caps its child's output, the session readers open the path their\n    containment check resolved, and a hook counts as wired only when a\n    command runs it.\n    \n    Floors held: typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35, scorer eval\n    [160,50,21,5]. Suite: 182 files, 1,744 passed. Doctor tests 1,188 and\n    reader tests 93, 0 failed.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation\n    Commit-Id: 0013831\n\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\nindex dad2d44b04..ceddc92c21 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n // MODULE: Hook Brief Signal/Noise Bench\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n-// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime (claude/opencode),\n+// Invokes the brief renderer per runtime (the iteration measured Claude and OpenCode, and the rest read not-recorded),\n // loads the iter-4 7-axis adapter divergence matrix as a fixture, and\n // asserts non-zero signal counts per runtime. Collector-shape coverage for\n // spec_kit.advisor.recommendation_emitted_total is kept separate from the\n@@ -24,8 +24,14 @@ const F22_AXES = [\n ] as const;\n \n const SEVEN_AXIS_MATRIX: Record<typeof ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES[number], Record<typeof F22_AXES[number], string>> = {\n-  claude:  { inputFieldNames: 'prompt-only', cwdResolution: 'input-or-process', inputSource: 'stdin-only', outputShape: 'hookSpecificOutput', timeoutHandling: 'none', renderThresholdOverride: 'none', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'none' },\n-  opencode:   { inputFieldNames: '3-fallbacks', cwdResolution: 'input-or-request-or-process', inputSource: 'stdin-or-argv', outputShape: 'hookSpecificOutput', timeoutHandling: 'env-3000ms', renderThresholdOverride: 'forced-0.8/0.35', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'none' },\n+  claude:   { inputFieldNames: 'prompt-only', cwdResolution: 'input-or-process', inputSource: 'stdin-only', outputShape: 'hookSpecificOutput', timeoutHandling: 'none', renderThresholdOverride: 'none', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'none' },\n+  opencode: { inputFieldNames: '3-fallbacks', cwdResolution: 'input-or-request-or-process', inputSource: 'stdin-or-argv', outputShape: 'hookSpecificOutput', timeoutHandling: 'env-3000ms', renderThresholdOverride: 'forced-0.8/0.35', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'none' },\n+  // An invented axis reading would pass for a measured one, so a runtime nobody probed reads not-recorded.\n+  pi:       { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n+  codex:    { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n+  cursor:   { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n+  devin:    { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n+  dsh:      { inputFieldNames: 'not-recorded', cwdResolution: 'not-recorded', inputSource: 'not-recorded', outputShape: 'not-recorded', timeoutHandling: 'not-recorded', renderThresholdOverride: 'not-recorded', sideEffectsBeyondReturn: 'not-recorded' },\n };\n \n function buildRecommendations(runtime: string): readonly AdvisorRecommendation[] {\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\nindex e8ea3e9d10..c98db0579c 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ Use this file to identify the folder boundary, the likely verification path and\n \n | Metric | Value |\n |---|---:|\n-| Code files | 9 |\n+| Code files | 14 |\n | README scope | Direct files in this folder |\n | Audit context | Internal validation notes |\n \n@@ -107,11 +107,24 @@ A typed command travels on its owner. It is delivered only when the leading reco\n | `gate3-corpus-runner.mjs` | MJS source file in this folder. |\n | `score-routing-corpus.py` | PY source file in this folder. |\n | `command-prompts.jsonl` | Prompt corpus with a gold slash command per row, covering every tracked command. |\n-| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. |\n-| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers on a turn whose brief arrived, `deliveryUnknown` counts rows whose brief state is `unknown`, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n+| `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` | Scores `command-prompts.jsonl` under the pinned regime and prints or writes the baseline. Its `attachedMetrics` key holds own-row, attached and combined plain reach per split and per command family, attached false offers, the typed rows where a command and its owner skill read as ambiguous, and the command attached to each published row. An attached hit counts only on a row the ranked bridge did not already land. Its `rows`, `attachedRows` and `typedRows` maps leave out every holdout row, so only holdout counts are published. The optional `--real-embedding` flag scores the same corpus against this machine's own skill graph database and live embedder in place of the fixture vectors and word overlap the default run substitutes, so its numbers describe an environment rather than a reproducible projection. It refuses `--write` because the committed baseline comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. Each row in its `rows` output also carries `offered`, which is true when any of the top three recommendations maps to a command bridge, so it measures reach rather than whether a brief head offered the command. |\n+| `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Each per-arm block reports `startRate`, `cappedStartRows`, `offered`, `cappedOfferRows`, `startedOfOffered`, `offerReached`, `deliveryUnknown`, `offerSeen`, `offerDeclined`, `offerFieldAbsent`, `unsafe`, `armIncomplete` and `byPolicy`, where `byPolicy` holds a `run`, `start` and `ask` tally of rows, capped rows, started rows and rows that wrote. `cappedOfferRows` counts offers whose turn hit its cap, `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so a row whose brief state is unknown counts, `deliveryUnknown` counts rows whose brief state is `unknown`, `offerSeen` and `offerDeclined` read the session's `COMMAND:` lines, and `offerFieldAbsent` counts rows that carry no offer field. `unsafe` also counts a workflow loop that started without its init, and a Claude turn that keeps only the `<command-name>` tag of a typed command counts as a start because Claude Code expands that command before the model sees it. The text output prints one `policy` line per policy under each arm. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n | `command-offer.mjs` | Recovers the attribution fields for a run line. `parseOffer` reads the command and policy out of one head, `replayOffer` replays a checkout's Claude prompt hook after the turn, `briefDelivered` reads the session record, and `backfillRunLog` writes the fields onto a finished log with a refusal code for a holdout, unknown or same-path input. |\n-| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n+| `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. `--backfill <run-log> --out <new-log> [--brief-only]` rewrites a finished log with `offeredCommand`, `offeredPolicy` and `briefDelivered` instead of running a turn, and prints a JSON refusal with `same_path`, `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when it cannot. After each turn it restores the checkout to HEAD and reports any `leftoverPaths` whose status still differs from the snapshot taken before the turn. Exit 3 (`head_moved`) ends the arm without that restore, because a commit or a stash made during the turn is not the runner's to discard, so the line records `restored: false` and the changed paths stay listed. A live turn gets only the allowlisted environment, the shell basics, the locale and XDG prefixes, each runtime's own prefixes and the Skilled switch prefixes, plus the GitHub and git overrides, so no GitHub token or git credential helper from the operator's shell reaches it. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`), a checkout without the arena builder's marker (`arena_unprepared`), or a Codex arm whose project hook is unapproved (`codex-hooks-unapproved`). |\n | `command-routing-baseline.json` | Captured command routing numbers that `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` holds the scorer to. |\n+| `build-holdout.mjs` | Builds the frozen holdout from three separately authored fixtures that are disjoint from the labeled corpus, copying each row's own label and keeping its provenance in `source_type` and `origin_fixture`. Family-normalized dedup keeps the first occurrence and drops any prompt that collides with the training corpus. `--write` rewrites `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. |\n+| `capture-local-native-divergence-ledger.mjs` | Recomputes the strict Python/native top-1 divergence set the ratchet replays. An existing approval is kept only while its prompt hash and both current tops still match, so the output is a capture of live scoring rather than a hand-edited fixture. Scores both scorers against a skill graph indexed fresh into a temporary directory with the clock pinned to the capture day, and `--write` records the result. |\n+| `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` | Captures scorer accuracy across the full corpus, the independent holdout, the frozen ambiguity slice and the named intent buckets under the reproducible filesystem projection, then `--write` records `scorer-eval-baseline.json`. Fixture hashes pin the baseline to the exact corpora it was captured against, so editing a fixture forces a conscious re-capture. `--misses` prints one failing prompt per line. |\n+| `derive-ambiguity-slice.mjs` | Derives the frozen ambiguity slice as the corpus rows whose top-2 fused-score margin is at or below `tau`, keeping each row's existing gold label, so a regression that only hurts contested prompts still fails a gate. `--write` rewrites `ambiguity-prompts.jsonl`, and the frozen `margin_at_capture` documents why a row is in the slice without being trusted by the gate. |\n+| `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` | Builds the arena a live arm runs in: a clone of the branch tip with no remote and no outer repository, plus the ignored build trees copied in and stamped at copy time so the freshness guard reads them as fresh. It refuses a destination inside a repository or one that already exists, and skips every file whose name begins with `.env` so no secret follows the build output in. |\n+| `reject-unknown-options.mjs` | Shared argument guard that exits 2 on the first token outside a script's declared option list, because silently ignoring a misspelled flag would run the default behavior and make the no-op look successful. |\n+| `score-outcome-rerank.mjs` | Measures whether the outcome-weighted rerank improves routing over the similarity-only ordering, reported as MRR and right-skill@3 rather than @1 alone. The reliability fold is built on a train split of the labeled corpus and accuracy is measured only on a disjoint held-out split, so memorized labels do not transfer. Read-only against the skill graph. |\n+| `worktree-restore.mjs` | Restores one measured turn's checkout to the snapshot taken before it, leaving a path that was already dirty alone and dropping a staged path HEAD does not know. A second snapshot after the restore reports what still differs, so the caller fails the run instead of claiming a clean worktree. |\n+| `ambiguity-prompts.jsonl` | Frozen ambiguity slice written by `derive-ambiguity-slice.mjs` and read by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`. Each row carries `id`, `prompt`, `skill_top_1`, `bucket`, `source_type`, `tau`, `margin_at_capture` and `captured_at`. |\n+| `doctor-prompts.jsonl` | Doctor routing slice read by `tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts`. Each row carries `id`, `prompt`, `expected_top`, `expected_second` and `wave`, where a wave scores only after every doctor bridge its rows expect is active, so a half-shipped bridge cannot fail the gate. |\n+| `holdout-prompts.jsonl` | Frozen holdout written by `build-holdout.mjs` from three separately authored fixtures disjoint from the labeled corpus, and read by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs` as its unseen split. |\n+| `labeled-prompts.jsonl` | Labeled training corpus with `id`, `prompt`, `skill_top_1`, `skill_correct`, `bucket`, `source_type`, `notes`, `gate3_triggers` and `gate3_reason_category`. Scored by `score-routing-corpus.py`, `score-outcome-rerank.mjs` and `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`, and read by the divergence ledger, the ambiguity deriver, the holdout builder and the gate 3 corpus runner. |\n+| `scorer-eval-baseline.json` | Scorer eval baseline written by `capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs`: `schemaVersion`, `capturedAt`, `capturedAtSha`, `env`, the fixture hashes and `metrics` for the full corpus, holdout, ambiguity slice, gold-none false fire, intent buckets and unknown count. The ratchet gate re-scores live under the same environment and holds every metric to it. |\n \n ---\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\nindex 9ed377507f..aba01f7013 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\n@@ -492,6 +492,9 @@ export async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n       // command, which the behaviour run line records as `offeredCommand`.\n       const offered = landed.some((command) => command !== null);\n       const isPlainSplit = row.row_type === 'plain' && (row.split === 'tune' || row.split === 'holdout');\n+      // A holdout row's outcome is what the split exists to keep unseen, so\n+      // only its counts are published.\n+      const publishRow = row.split !== 'holdout';\n \n       // A hub can name the slash command its route would take, which is reach a\n       // reader otherwise gets only by translating the workflow mode by hand.\n@@ -509,13 +512,15 @@ export async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n       if (row.row_type === 'typed') {\n         addRow(typed, top1Hit, top3Hit);\n         addAttachedRow(typedAttached, top1Hit, deliveredHit);\n-        typedRowResults[row.id] = {\n-          expected_command: expected,\n-          top: ids[0] ?? null,\n-          carried: top1Hit ? 'own' : deliveredHit ? 'attached' : null,\n-          command: delivered ?? null,\n-          policy: deliveredPolicy,\n-        };\n+        if (publishRow) {\n+          typedRowResults[row.id] = {\n+            expected_command: expected,\n+            top: ids[0] ?? null,\n+            carried: top1Hit ? 'own' : deliveredHit ? 'attached' : null,\n+            command: delivered ?? null,\n+            policy: deliveredPolicy,\n+          };\n+        }\n       }\n       if (isPlainSplit) {\n         addRow(plain[row.split], top1Hit, top3Hit);\n@@ -523,7 +528,7 @@ export async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n         const family = attachedFamilyTally(plainAttachedByFamily, expected);\n         if (family) addAttachedRow(family[row.split], top1Hit, attachedHit);\n       }\n-      if (attached !== undefined) attachedRows[row.id] = attached;\n+      if (publishRow && attached !== undefined) attachedRows[row.id] = attached;\n       if (row.row_type === 'typed' && result?.ambiguous === true && isBridgeOwnerPair(idToCommand, ids, expected)) {\n         sameOwnerAmbiguous.push(row.id);\n       }\n@@ -534,7 +539,9 @@ export async function scoreCommandCorpus(options = {}) {\n         else if (isPlainSplit) addRow(commandTally.plain[row.split], top1Hit, top3Hit);\n       }\n \n-      rows[row.id] = { expected_command: expected, top: ids[0] ?? null, top1: top1Hit, top3: top3Hit, offered };\n+      if (publishRow) {\n+        rows[row.id] = { expected_command: expected, top: ids[0] ?? null, top1: top1Hit, top3: top3Hit, offered };\n+      }\n \n       const isSlashVariant = row.row_type === 'slash-variant';\n       // Silence is the requirement for a near miss, a prompt that must not\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\nindex 1c9fb9885f..eec4bce796 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n {\n   \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n   \"capturedAt\": \"2026-10-11\",\n-  \"capturedAtSha\": \"99b68d8b3d\",\n+  \"capturedAtSha\": \"320e7b64d4\",\n   \"corpusSha256\": \"sha256:698da57b02159a756dbba5d6a2c9a3c6d14588d07e96be268567835cf36448b8\",\n   \"bridgeCounts\": {\n     \"commandMetadata\": 27,\n@@ -933,13 +933,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-agent-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:agent\",\n-      \"top\": \"sk-code\",\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-benchmark-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:benchmark\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -954,13 +947,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-benchmark-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:benchmark\",\n-      \"top\": null,\n-      \"top1\": false,\n-      \"top3\": false,\n-      \"offered\": false\n-    },\n     \"cmd-create-changelog-typed-01\": {\n       \"expected_command\": \"/create:changelog\",\n       \"top\": \"sk-doc\",\n@@ -975,13 +961,6 @@\n       \"top3\": false,\n       \"offered\": false\n     },\n-    \"cmd-create-changelog-plain-holdout-01\": {\n-      \"expected_command\": \"/create:chan