\n\n    docs(specs): record review pass one, research segment three and the phase 015 plan\n    \n    Review pass one over the command surfacing code: four lineages, 43\n    confirmed findings in 14 work groups, 0 P0 and 0 P1 after verification.\n    Research segment three: three lineages and 16 ranked recommendations\n    with their dispositions. The final behaviour arm at 320e7b64d4 with its\n    scored summary. The plan for phase 015, which builds segment three\n    ranks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9 and 11. The parent phase map gains phases 014\n    and 015, and the goal log carries each decision and each item waiting\n    on the operator.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\n    Commit-Id: 0013832\n\ndiff --git a/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md b/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md\nindex fbd94f27a9..868bf1c434 100644\n--- a/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md\n+++ b/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md\n@@ -126,6 +126,8 @@ Audit trail only. Each child's `plan.md` holds the detail, and phases 5 to 7 are\n | 11 | 011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/ | Every typed tracked command reaches the model on the top recommendation with its command and policy, measured as 44 of 44 typed rows in the command capture, plus a command visibility guard in the mirror check, hook health in the advisor status and a head length test with a brief cost script (research ranks 9, 12 and 14 in part) | Complete |\n | 12 | 012-plain-offer-reach/ | A plain request gets its command: the doctor hand-off names the command its ranker put first, task-shaped aliases on the `sk-doc` and deep-loop hubs, deep and create anchors and a `(needs a mode)` label for a deferring hub, measured as plain tune offers 9 to 23 of 45 in the command capture (segment two ranks 1, 4, 6, 7 and 12) | Complete |\n | 13 | 013-attribution-and-install-reach/ | Brief delivery as a stored fact on five runtimes, offer accounting with loop-without-init in the safety floor and host-expanded typed starts counted, a Codex preflight and a restore to HEAD in the behaviour runner, a `CLAUDE.md` pointer on the default embed install, a delivery leg in `/doctor:setup` and an OpenCode brief that keeps the command fields (segment two ranks 2, 3, 5, 8 to 11 and 13) | Complete |\n+| 14 | 014-review-remediation/ | The fixes for review pass one: 43 confirmed items in 13 file-disjoint work groups, with the embed write safety, the attach-path guards, the renderer contract and the behaviour runner containment first, so a second review pass can run on the fixed code (review/review-report.md) | In Progress |\n+| 15 | 015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/ | A prompt-free hook health record by default with a degraded flag and the newest record time, the `(needs a mode)` label only when the prompt names the hub, the top hub naming its routed command, no compiled-route line in the OpenCode brief, a brief-cost script that reads live heads only and three behaviour-arm counts (segment three ranks 1 to 5, 9 and 11) | Planned |\n \n ### Phase Transition Rules\n \n@@ -147,6 +149,8 @@ Audit trail only. Each child's `plan.md` holds the detail, and phases 5 to 7 are\n | 007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof | 008-embedder-setup-and-cost | Phase 005 is merged and the per-runtime proof is recorded, so this phase edits the final recommendation handler and bridge activation list | `rg -n \"ownerSkillId\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts` prints a line and phase 007 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\n | 011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards | 012-plain-offer-reach | Phase 011 is committed, the command capture reads 44 of 44 typed rows and every pinned floor holds | `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts