{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571167560,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c6e414001FqI6unI0TzcZ32","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","messageID":"msg_1d4c6cd9b001BPhrD08Vtj48IY","type":"tool","id":"call_e46fdf82005f44cca0685918","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime; sed -n '160,230p' tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts; echo \"=== README 150-165 ===\"; sed -n '145,165p' tests/README.md"},"output":"    expect(live.corpusSha256).toBe(baseline.corpusSha256);\n  });\n\n  it('has a typed row and both plain splits for every command file', () => {\n    // A command with an empty split carries no evidence either way, so its\n    // recall reads as a pass while the corpus never exercised it.\n    const uncovered = Object.keys(live.commands).filter((command) => {\n      const tally = live.commands[command];\n      return tally.typed.rows < 1 || tally.plain.tune.rows < 1 || tally.plain.holdout.rows < 1;\n    });\n    expect(uncovered).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n=== README 150-165 ===\n## 5. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `lane-attribution.test.ts` | Verifies prompt-safe lane attribution behavior. |\n| `affordance-normalizer.test.ts` | Tests affordance normalization used by advisor routing. |\n| `routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts` | Connects fixture prompts to affordance expectations. |\n| `shadow-sink.vitest.ts` | Covers shadow telemetry sink behavior. |\n| `skill-graph-db.vitest.ts` | Checks skill-graph database behavior used by advisor tests. |\n| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures. |\n| `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | Verifies the stale-daemon retry in the CLI entrypoint. |\n| `prompt-policy-gold-replay.vitest.ts` | Replays the prompt gate over the labeled and golden corpora. |\n| `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 17 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n| `command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` | Pins the `derivePolicy` ladder and the closed risk-key vocabularies, and checks that the command tree and its declarations agree. |\n| `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Holds live command routing to `scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` row by row, pins the corpus hash and requires a typed row and both plain splits for every command file. |\n| `embedders/` | Covers embedder schema, registry and shared-factory parity. |\n| `skill-graph/` | Covers focused skill-graph refresh round trips. |\n| `tsconfig.tests.json` | Type-checks the CLI and launcher test files listed in its `include`, extending the runtime `tsconfig.json`, with no emit. |\n\n---\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    expect(live.corpusSha256).toBe(baseline.corpusSha256);\n  });\n\n  it('has a typed row and both plain splits for every command file', () => {\n    // A command with an empty split carries no evidence either way, so its\n    // recall reads as a pass while the corpus never exercised it.\n    const uncovered = Object.keys(live.commands).filter((command) => {\n      const tally = live.commands[command];\n      return tally.typed.rows < 1 || tally.plain.tune.rows < 1 || tally.plain.holdout.rows < 1;\n    });\n    expect(uncovered).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n=== README 150-165 ===\n## 5. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `lane-attribution.test.ts` | Verifies prompt-safe lane attribution behavior. |\n| `affordance-normalizer.test.ts` | Tests affordance normalization used by advisor routing. |\n| `routing-fixtures.affordance.test.ts` | Connects fixture prompts to affordance expectations. |\n| `shadow-sink.vitest.ts` | Covers shadow telemetry sink behavior. |\n| `skill-graph-db.vitest.ts` | Checks skill-graph database behavior used by advisor tests. |\n| `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts` | Verifies manual testing playbook routing fixtures. |\n| `skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | Verifies the stale-daemon retry in the CLI entrypoint. |\n| `prompt-policy-gold-replay.vitest.ts` | Replays the prompt gate over the labeled and golden corpora. |\n| `command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | 17 cases on the meaning way in for a command row: a real cosine has to clear the bar and lead the other command rows by the margin, stand-in evidence never passes, a skill row is left alone, a meaning-passed command moves ahead of a passing skill only by the margin, and eligibility rules out every command on a no-edit request and all but read-only commands on a read-only question. |\n| `command-policy-derivation.vitest.ts` | Pins the `derivePolicy` ladder and the closed risk-key vocabularies, and checks that the command tree and its declarations agree. |\n| `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` | Holds live command routing to `scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` row by row, pins the corpus hash and requires a typed row and both plain splits for every command file. |\n| `embedders/` | Covers embedder schema, registry and shared-factory parity. |\n| `skill-graph/` | Covers focused skill-graph refresh round trips. |\n| `tsconfig.tests.json` | Type-checks the CLI and launcher test files listed in its `include`, extending the runtime `tsconfig.json`, with no emit. |\n\n---\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime; sed -n '160,230p' tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts; echo \\\"=== README 150-165 ===\\\"; sed -n '145,165p' tests/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571166740,"end":1794571167560}}}}
