{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571302587,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c8edc0001hKCmK6YJ79zpFj","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","messageID":"msg_1d4c8df1a0011O3MrcM12rPouv","type":"tool","id":"call_484da5498a5d4ec2b18f3772","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Re-reading each fix at its cited line and then running the two guard files turned the fix replay into observed evidence instead of a doc comparison (iteration 1).\n- Counting the corpus and baseline by `id`, `split` and `row_type` proved holdout hygiene without ever printing prompt text (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- The phase-map fix cannot be confirmed from the parent map: its reason sits only in `007/tasks.md`, so the pass-one item is reported again rather than closed (iteration 1).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -70,16 +70,15 @@\n \n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n-- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n+- Re-reading each fix at its cited line and then running the two guard files turned the fix replay into observed evidence instead of a doc comparison (iteration 1).\n+- Counting the corpus and baseline by `id`, `split` and `row_type` proved holdout hygiene without ever printing prompt text (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n-- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n+- The phase-map fix cannot be confirmed from the parent map: its reason sits only in `007/tasks.md`, so the pass-one item is reported again rather than closed (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":4}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n- Re-reading each fix at its cited line and then running the two guard files turned the fix replay into observed evidence instead of a doc comparison (iteration 1).\\n- Counting the corpus and baseline by `id`, `split` and `row_type` proved holdout hygiene without ever printing prompt text (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n- The phase-map fix cannot be confirmed from the parent map: its reason sits only in `007/tasks.md`, so the pass-one item is reported again rather than closed (iteration 1).\",\"oldString\":\"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n- [Approach]: [Why it w