{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571733607,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4cf838b001zG3Om71Zez3Nmd","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","messageID":"msg_1d4cf3d880010prZBVeJo2Kzlm","type":"tool","id":"call_59e0f3101b9f44a699725fc0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor; grep -n \"routing-accuracy\\|behaviour runner\\|manual-testing-playbook\" feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md feature-catalog/cli-surface/*.md feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -15; echo \"=== README 176 ===\"; sed -n '172,180p' README.md; echo \"=== count command rows ===\"; node -e 'const fs=require(\"fs\");const b=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\",\"utf8\"));console.log(Object.keys(b.commands).length)'"},"output":"feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:73:| `Playbook scenarios [NC-001](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/native-recommend-happy-path.md), [NC-004](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/ambiguous-brief-rendering.md), [NC-005](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/lifecycle-redirect-metadata.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-status.md:56:| `Playbook scenario [NC-002](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/native-status-transitions.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-validate.md:82:| `Playbook scenario [NC-003](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/native-validate-slices.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/cli-surface/compat-entrypoint.md:53:| `Playbook scenarios [CL-005](../../manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/opencode-plugin-bridge.md) and [CP-001..CP-004](../../manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/cli-surface/skill-advisor-cli.md:79:- Playbook counterparts: scenario CL-006 in `../../manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` plus spec-kit playbook scenarios 427, 431, 432, and 438\nfeature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:60:| `Playbook scenario [CL-001](../../manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/goal-opencode-plugin.md:73:| `manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/goal-opencode-plugin.md` | Manual playbook | Operator scenario for `/goal` command and plugin behavior |\nfeature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/opencode-plugin-bridge.md:57:| `Playbook scenario [CL-005](../../manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/opencode-plugin-bridge.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\n=== README 176 ===\n### The Embedder\n\nThe `semantic_shadow` lane runs against the pluggable embedder layer in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor owns. The registry holds text-tuned embedding models and defaults through a local-first cascade to a local model when no embedder is explicitly set. For the full model registry, the cascade tier table and the swap workflow, see `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §12.\n\nCommand rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n\n### The Nine Commands\n\nThe CLI exposes nine commands, each accepting snake case, kebab case and camel case spellings. `list-tools` enumerates all nine. `skill_graph_propagate_enhances` is only trust-gated for the mutating apply path. Report, propose, dry-run apply stay read-safe. You have already met the first three in Quick Start.\n=== count command rows ===\n44\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:73:| `Playbook scenarios [NC-001](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/native-recommend-happy-path.md), [NC-004](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/ambiguous-brief-rendering.md), [NC-005](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/lifecycle-redirect-metadata.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-status.md:56:| `Playbook scenario [NC-002](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/native-status-transitions.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-validate.md:82:| `Playbook scenario [NC-003](../../manual-testing-playbook/native-cli-tools/native-validate-slices.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/cli-surface/compat-entrypoint.md:53:| `Playbook scenarios [CL-005](../../manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/opencode-plugin-bridge.md) and [CP-001..CP-004](../../manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/cli-surface/skill-advisor-cli.md:79:- Playbook counterparts: scenario CL-006 in `../../manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` plus spec-kit playbook scenarios 427, 431, 432, and 438\nfeature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:60:| `Playbook scenario [CL-001](../../manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/claude-user-prompt-submit.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\nfeature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/goal-opencode-plugin.md:73:| `manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/goal-opencode-plugin.md` | Manual playbook | Operator scenario for `/goal` command and plugin behavior |\nfeature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/opencode-plugin-bridge.md:57:| `Playbook scenario [CL-005](../../manual-testing-playbook/cli-hooks-and-plugin/opencode-plugin-bridge.md).` | Manual playbook | Source reference |\n=== README 176 ===\n### The Embedder\n\nThe `semantic_shadow` lane runs against the pluggable embedder layer in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor owns. The registry holds text-tuned embedding models and defaults through a local-first cascade to a local model when no embedder is explicitly set. For the full model registry, the cascade tier table and the swap workflow, see `INSTALL-GUIDE.md` §12.\n\nCommand rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n\n### The Nine Commands\n\nThe CLI exposes nine commands, each accepting snake case, kebab case and camel case spellings. `list-tools` enumerates all nine. `skill_graph_propagate_enhances` is only trust-gated for the mutating apply path. Report, propose, dry-run apply stay read-safe. You have already met the first three in Quick Start.\n=== count command rows ===\n44\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor; grep -n \\\"routing-accuracy\\\\|behaviour runner\\\\|manual-testing-playbook\\\" feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md feature-catalog/cli-surface/*.md feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/*.md 2>/dev/null | head -15; echo \\\"=== README 176 ===\\\"; sed -n '172,180p' README.md; echo \\\"=== count command rows ===\\\"; node -e 'const fs=require(\\\"fs\\\");const b=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(\\\"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json\\\",\\\"utf8\\\"));console.log(Object.keys(b.commands).length)'\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571731851,"end":1794571733607}}}}
