{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794572268004,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4d75d11001qmwQ8bGKGYlVFt","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","messageID":"msg_1d4d748a0001aoBj3JSw40nJGY","type":"tool","id":"call_7b13ba45626a444b82f6bc60","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 007\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-2`, pass two)\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Dimension: adjudication across all four dimensions\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Budget profile: adjudicate (9 review actions)\n- Operator review focus bound as `review_focus`: pass-two review of command surfacing in the `accuracy-runner` area; confirm the final severity and wording of every active finding, and make sure no P0 or P1 is hidden behind an advisory.\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it re-read every active P2's case and evidence, checked that no finding sits outside the declared area or depends on inference alone, confirmed the pass-one deferred and refuted items were not re-reported, and evaluated the stop condition. The loop reaches `maxIterations=7` without a legal graph-backed STOP, exactly as the pass-one lineages did, so the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`.\n- `steer.md`: absent before this iteration; no lead rulings to apply.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- All twelve active finding lines, re-read at iteration 6 and cross-checked here against the finding text.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` (counts only)\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:394-404` (deferred items, checked for non-duplication)\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone new. Twelve P2s are active from iterations 1 to 5; their adjudication is below.\n\n## Adjudication of Active P2s\n\nAll twelve are confirmed at P2 with `file:line` evidence and a concrete case. None is inference-only, none sits outside the area, and none is a re-report of a pass-one finding whose fix holds or of a section-8 deferred item.\n\n| # | Finding | Evidence | Case check | Severity check |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence` | `spec.md:122`; `007/tasks.md:141` | Parent-map reader cannot tell why 007 is open | P2: navigation, not a wrong result |\n| 2 | `iter2-P2-g2-row-id-arm-mislabel` | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:974,1232` | `--row-id g2-...` logs arm `pre` | P2: a mislabeled measurement, no data loss |\n| 3 | `iter2-P2-backfill-fixture-mismatch` | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:793-803,1213-1220` | custom `--fixture` replays the default path | P2: backfill is a diagnostic path |\n| 4 | `iter2-P2-capture-env-not-restored` | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:361-377,662-668` | second in-process score inherits a deleted db dir | P2: in-process harness only |\n| 5 | `iter2-P2-cost-script-child-brief` | `measure-brief-cost.mjs:167`; `render.ts:533` | `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` measures the child brief | P2: dispatched-worker context |\n| 6 | `iter3-P2-backfill-log-code-execution` | `command-offer.mjs:333,406-428` | crafted log's `projectDir` runs its hook | P2: needs an untrusted log and a crafted directory |\n| 7 | `iter4-P2-playbook-inventory-note` | `manual-testing-playbook.md:40` | reader sees 41 `NNN-*.md` against 50 files | P2: documentation drift |\n| 8 | `iter4-P2-playbook-persistence-path` | `manual-testing-playbook.md:30` | `benchmark/reports/` does not exist under the skill | P2: documentation drift |\n| 9 | `iter4-P2-tests-readme-description` | `runtime/tests/README.md:154` | table misdescribes the inventory test | P2: maintainer navigation |\n| 10 | `iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode` | `README.md:112`; `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1455` | `--row-id` accepted and ignored in session mode | P2: silent flag |\n| 11 | `iter5-P2-quoted-path-restore` | `worktree-restore.mjs:54,79` | a file with a space cannot be restored, arm stops | P2: fails safe, blocks the next arm |\n| 12 | `iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report` | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:5-9` | header promises an ordered report the CLI never prints | P2: maintainer time |\n\nSeverity checks applied: none of the twelve crosses a trust boundary in a default path (findings 6 and 11 are the closest, and both need a non-default input), none leaves a wrong score silently (11 fails the arm; 6 is a local backfill tool), and none blocks release by itself. Finding 2 is the only one that can put a wrong number in front of a reader on a default path **if** the operator selects a g2 row by id, which the CLI documents as supported; it still mislabels rather than fails, so P2 stands.\n\n## Pass-One Non-Duplication Check\n\n- No re-report of a pass-one finding whose fix holds: the fix replay in iteration 1 covers all nine items and only the phase-map partial is reported.\n- No report of section-8 deferred items: the `run`-writes decision, the dsh install path, the sandboxed-runtime reach, the DSH `source` reach and the third no-edit pattern are untouched.\n- No report of `R4-P2-003` (the AGENTS.md edit that waits on the operator) or of the refuted finding.\n- The four doc findings are new; none of them is a rewrite of a pass-one item.\n\n## Stop Evaluation\n\n- Iterations dispatched: 7. `maxIterations=7` is reached, so the workflow's hard stop applies with `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\n- The coverage graph is unavailable for this lineage (`graphCoverageMode: graphless_fallback`), so the graph prerequisite cannot return `STOP_ALLOWED`; a legal graph-backed STOP is not claimed.\n- Dimension coverage: correctness (iterations 1-2), security (3), traceability (4), maintainability (5), stabilization (6), adjudication (7). Required traceability protocols: `spec_code` pass, `checklist_evidence` partial with a named packet gap, overlays recorded.\n- Active findings: P0=0, P1=0, P2=12. The verdict mapping is therefore PASS with `hasAdvisories=true`.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code`: pass. Five floors and the pinned clock re-derived.\n- `checklist_evidence`: partial. Phase 007's T020/T046 and AC-004/005/007 remain open; the parent map note is finding 1.\n- `skill_agent`: notApplicable.\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: partial. Read evidence for six runtimes; live proof stays phase 007's.\n- `feature_catalog_code`: pass.\n- `playbook_capability`: partial. NC-011 holds; the root playbook carries findings 7 and 8.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The terminal record and this narrative agree on counts (12 active P2, 0 P0, 0 P1) and on the stop reason; the reducer's registry is the record the merge reads.\n- The synthesis report will restate the same counts from the registry, not from this prose.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **The loop stops at the cap, not at legal convergence.** Pass one did the same for every lineage because the graph was unavailable; the report must say so rather than claim convergence.\n- **Findings 2-6 and 11 are code-shaped and cheap to fix**, but this review changes no code; they stay advisories for the remediation owner.\n- **No live arm and no graph.** Both limits are recorded on every iteration that depended on them.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The verdict mapping: no active P0 or P1, so PASS with advisories.\n- The finding registry's counts match the iteration records.\n- No file outside the lineage was modified by this review; the only writes are the iteration, delta, strategy, registry/dashboard, and report artifacts inside the lineage.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **Holding a P2 as a P1 to make the report look thorough.** Rejected: every P2's reach was tested, and the two closest (log-path execution, quoted-path restore) need a non-default input.\n- **Calling the run converged.** Rejected: the graph-backed STOP was unavailable and the cap was reached.\n- **Re-opening the pass-one credential and holdout items at P1.** Rejected: the fixes hold and the replay rows pass with evidence.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: synthesis\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry and the seven iteration files, then let the cross-lineage merge recompute the merged verdict\n- Reason: the cap is reached; no further iteration can change the active set without new evidence\n- Rotation status: all dimensions complete, stabilization and adjudication done\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: blocked (no live arm, no graph); productive (fix replay, doc/tree comparison, restore probe)\n- Required evidence: the report's counts equal the registry's, and the final line is exactly one verdict\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-007.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-007.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-007.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 007\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `accuracy-runner-2`, pass two)\\n- Session: `fanout-accuracy-runner-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Dimension: adjudication across all four dimensions\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Budget profile: adjudicate (9 review actions)\\n- Operator review focus bound as `review_focus`: pass-two review of command surfacing in the `accuracy-runner` area; confirm the final severity and wording of every active finding, and make sure no P0 or P1 is hidden behind an advisory.\\n- How this iteration addressed the focus: it re-read every active P2's case and evidence, checked that no finding sits outside the declared area or depends on inference alone, confirmed the pass-one deferred and refuted items were not re-reported, and evaluated the stop condition. The loop reaches `maxIterations=7` without a legal graph-backed STOP, exactly as the pass-one lineages did, so the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`.\\n- `steer.md`: absent before this iteration; no lead rulings to apply.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- All twelve active finding lines, re-read at iteration 6 and cross-checked here against the finding text.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json` (counts only)\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:394-404` (deferred items, checked for non-duplication)\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone new. Twelve P2s are active from iterations 1 to 5; their adjudication is below.\\n\\n## Adjudication of Active P2s\\n\\nAll twelve are confirmed at P2 with `file:line` evidence and a concrete case. None is inference-only, none sits outside the area, and none is a re-report of a pass-one finding whose fix holds or of a section-8 deferred item.\\n\\n| # | Finding | Evidence | Case check | Severity check |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | `iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence` | `spec.md:122`; `007/tasks.md:141` | Parent-map reader cannot tell why 007 is open | P2: navigation, not a wrong result |\\n| 2 | `iter2-P2-g2-row-id-arm-mislabel` | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:974,1232` | `--row-id g2-...` logs arm `pre` | P2: a mislabeled measurement, no data loss |\\n| 3 | `iter2-P2-backfill-fixture-mismatch` | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:793-803,1213-1220` | custom `--fixture` replays the default path | P2: backfill is a diagnostic path |\\n| 4 | `iter2-P2-capture-env-not-restored` | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:361-377,662-668` | second in-process score inherits a deleted db dir | P2: in-process harness only |\\n| 5 | `iter2-P2-cost-script-child-brief` | `measure-brief-cost.mjs:167`; `render.ts:533` | `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` measures the child brief | P2: dispatched-worker context |\\n| 6 | `iter3-P2-backfill-log-code-execution` | `command-offer.mjs:333,406-428` | crafted log's `projectDir` runs its hook | P2: needs an untrusted log and a crafted directory |\\n| 7 | `iter4-P2-playbook-inventory-note` | `manual-testing-playbook.md:40` | reader sees 41 `NNN-*.md` against 50 files | P2: documentation drift |\\n| 8 | `iter4-P2-playbook-persistence-path` | `manual-testing-playbook.md:30` | `benchmark/reports/` does not exist under the skill | P2: documentation drift |\\n| 9 | `iter4-P2-tests-readme-description` | `runtime/tests/README.md:154` | table misdescribes the inventory test | P2: maintainer navigation |\\n| 10 | `iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode` | `README.md:112`; `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1455` | `--row-id` accepted and ignored in session mode | P2: silent flag |\\n| 11 | `iter5-P2-quoted-path-restore` | `worktree-restore.mjs:54,79` | a file with a space cannot be restored, arm stops | P2: fails safe, blocks the next arm |\\n| 12 | `iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report` | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:5-9` | header promises an ordered report the CLI never prints | P2: maintainer time |\\n\\nSeverity checks applied: none of the twelve crosses a trust boundary in a default path (findings 6 and 11 are the closest, and both need a non-default input), none leaves a wrong score silently (11 fails the arm; 6 is a local backfill tool), and none blocks release by itself. Finding 2 is the only one that can put a wrong number in front of a reader on a default path **if** the operator selects a g2 row by id, which the CLI documents as supported; it still mislabels rather than fails, so P2 stands.\\n\\n## Pass-One Non-Duplication Check\\n\\n- No re-report of a pass-one finding whose fix holds: the fix replay in iteration 1 covers all nine items and only the phase-map partial is reported.\\n- No report of section-8 deferred items: the `run`-writes decision, the dsh install path, the sandboxed-runtime reach, the DSH `source` reach and the third no-edit pattern are untouched.\\n- No report of `R4-P2-003` (the AGENTS.md edit that waits on the operator) or of the refuted finding.\\n- The four doc findings are new; none of them is a rewrite of a pass-one item.\\n\\n## Stop Evaluation\\n\\n- Iterations dispatched: 7. `maxIterations=7` is reached, so the workflow's hard stop applies with `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\\n- The coverage graph is unavailable for this lineage (`graphCoverageMode: graphless_fallback`), so the graph prerequisite cannot return `STOP_ALLOWED`; a legal graph-backed STOP is not claimed.\\n- Dimension coverage: correctness (iterations 1-2), security (3), traceability (4), maintainability (5), stabilization (6), adjudication (7). Required traceability protocols: `spec_code` pass, `checklist_evidence` partial with a named packet gap, overlays recorded.\\n- Active findings: P0=0, P1=0, P2=12. The verdict mapping is therefore PASS with `hasAdvisories=true`.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code`: pass. Five floors and the pinned clock re-derived.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: partial. Phase 007's T020/T046 and AC-004/005/007 remain open; the parent map note is finding 1.\\n- `skill_agent`: notApplicable.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: partial. Read evidence for six runtimes; live proof stays phase 007's.\\n- `feature_catalog_code`: pass.\\n- `playbook_capability`: partial. NC-011 holds; the root playbook carries findings 7 and 8.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The terminal record and this narrative agree on counts (12 active P2, 0 P0, 0 P1) and on the stop reason; the reducer's registry is the record the merge reads.\\n- The synthesis report will restate the same counts from the registry, not from this prose.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **The loop stops at the cap, not at legal convergence.** Pass one did the same for every lineage because the graph was unavailable; the report must say so rather than claim convergence.\\n- **Findings 2-6 and 11 are code-shaped and cheap to fix**, but this review changes no code; they stay advisories for the remediation owner.\\n- **No live arm and no graph.** Both limits are recorded on every iteration that depended on them.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The verdict mapping: no active P0 or P1, so PASS with advisories.\\n- The finding registry's counts match the iteration records.\\n- No file outside the lineage was modified by this review; the only writes are the iteration, delta, strategy, registry/dashboard, and report artifacts inside the lineage.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **Holding a P2 as a P1 to make the report look thorough.** Rejected: every P2's reach was tested, and the two closest (log-path execution, quoted-path restore) need a non-default input.\\n- **Calling the run converged.** Rejected: the graph-backed STOP was unavailable and the cap was reached.\\n- **Re-opening the pass-one credential and holdout items at P1.** Rejected: the fixes hold and the replay rows pass with evidence.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: synthesis\\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry and the seven iteration files, then let the cross-lineage merge recompute the merged verdict\\n- Reason: the cap is reached; no further iteration can change the active set without new evidence\\n- Rotation status: all dimensions complete, stabilization and adjudication done\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: blocked (no live arm, no graph); productive (fix replay, doc/tree comparison, restore probe)\\n- Required evidence: the report's counts equal the registry's, and the final line is exactly one verdict\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/iterations/iteration-007.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794572246289,"end":1794572268004}}}}
