{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794572417195,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4d95f70002tQt3kuyrc1ac4V","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a2200ffebIrmmKNfkMdQAD","messageID":"msg_1d4d9440f001EddQ6GHc1xsGWP","type":"tool","id":"call_af69ea1ae08d482e8ac655da","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build — accuracy-runner-2 (pass two)\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: lineage=accuracy-runner-2; sessionId=fanout-accuracy-runner-2-1794570021136-noekp0; generation=1; lineageMode=new; stopReason=maxIterationsReached -->\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict:** PASS\n- **hasAdvisories:** true\n- **Active findings:** P0 = 0, P1 = 0, P2 = 12\n- **Review scope:** the pass-two `accuracy-runner` area of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`: the routing-accuracy harness, prompt corpora and committed baselines, transcript and offer tests, cost measurements, legacy fidelity tests and the manual-testing playbook. 31 area files plus the shared docs that describe them; 13 area files changed since pass one and 18 unchanged.\n- **Operator review focus:** Code review of command surfacing, PASS TWO. First read the full instructions in the pass-two instructions file and follow them: for each pass-one finding in the accuracy-runner area, re-read the code and say whether the fix holds; review every file marked yes (changed since pass one) line by line for a defect the fix introduced; then look for new defects. Scope file lists area, path and changed-since-pass-one. Check behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene, so no tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows; docs that disagree with code. Never read or print holdout prompt text (split holdout in command-prompts.jsonl, or holdout-prompts.jsonl): counts only. Change no code, write only inside the lineage folder.\n- **Headline:** eight of the nine pass-one findings this lineage raised hold; the ninth (the parent phase map) is only half fixed and is reported again. The changed code introduced no new P0 or P1. The pass-two findings are ten P2s about measurement attribution, process isolation, a run-log trust boundary, a restore edge, and four docs that disagree with the tree or the code.\n- **Loop state:** `maxIterations=7` reached; the coverage graph was unavailable, so a legal graph-backed STOP was not claimable. Release readiness is `in-progress`, not `converged`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for this lineage: there is no active P0, no active P1 and no failed binary gate. The twelve P2s are advisories for the remediation owner.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": false,\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n  \"activeFindings\": 12,\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": 4,\n  \"specSeed\": [\"Close or annotate phase 007 in the parent phase map\", \"Correct the manual-testing-playbook inventory note, persistence path and tests-README description\"],\n  \"planSeed\": [\"Fix the four harness advisories in one small group\", \"Add the missing tests named in the registry\"],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"measurement-correctness\", \"process-isolation\", \"security\", \"traceability\", \"maintainability\", \"correctness\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy\", \"runtime/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs\", \"manual-testing-playbook\", \"runtime/tests/README.md\", \"spec.md\"],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Sev | Title | Dimension | File:line | Evidence | Impact | Fix recommendation | Disposition | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surfaces |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence` | P2 | The pass-one phase-map finding is only half fixed: the reason lives in the phase child, not in the map the finding named | traceability | `spec.md:122` | Row 7 `In Progress` beside completed 008 and 010-013; reason only at `007/tasks.md:141` | A parent-map reader cannot tell an intentional deferral from a skipped phase | Add one sentence to row 7 or a note under the map naming the final behaviour arm | Active | traceability | Packet spec is the review target; the item was raised by this lineage | `spec.md`; `007/tasks.md:141` |\n| `iter2-P2-g2-row-id-arm-mislabel` | P2 | A started-command row selected by `--row-id` is logged under the `pre` arm | correctness | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:974` | `armFor` keys only on `options.set`; `assertRunnable` accepts g2 ids | A 15-minute g2 turn joins the pre arm and skews the comparison | Derive the arm from the row id when the set is absent, or refuse `--row-id` g2 ids without `--arm` | Active | measurement-correctness | Runner and scorer in scope | run line; scorer bucketing |\n| `iter2-P2-backfill-fixture-mismatch` | P2 | `--backfill` replays a g2 row with the default fixture even when the run used a custom one | correctness | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1214` | Run uses `options.fixture`; backfill re-derives `g2-fixture` from its own log path | The replayed offer describes a prompt the turn never ran | Record the fixture path on the run line or add `--fixture` to the backfill | Active | measurement-correctness | Runner and backfill in scope | run log; `command-offer.mjs` backfill |\n| `iter2-P2-capture-env-not-restored` | P2 | The capture leaves its environment projection installed after it returns | correctness | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:361` | Five env vars written and four deleted; `finally` restores only `Date` and removes the temp dir | A second in-process score inherits a deleted DB dir and the fixture regime | Snapshot and restore `process.env` in the `finally` | Active | process-isolation | Capture module and its in-process caller | capture; slice test |\n| `iter2-P2-cost-script-child-brief` | P2 | `measure-brief-cost.mjs` measures the child-session brief from a dispatched worker | correctness | `measure-brief-cost.mjs:167` | Hook env spreads `process.env`; renderer reads `AI_SESSION_CHILD` | The reported cost is the child brief, not the user brief | Strip `AI_SESSION_CHILD` (and state it) before spawning the hook | Active | measurement-correctness | Cost script and renderer branch | cost figures |\n| `iter3-P2-backfill-log-code-execution` | P2 | `--backfill` executes the hook and advisor CLI from the directory a log line names | security | `command-offer.mjs:333` | `checkoutDir` comes from `locator.projectDir`; `warmCheckout` and `replayOffer` spawn from it | A crafted log selects the JavaScript the backfill runs | Require the log's directory to equal the audited checkout, or refuse a path outside the repo | Active | security | Backfill and its caller | backfill path |\n| `iter4-P2-playbook-inventory-note` | P2 | The playbook's coverage note names a file convention and count the tree does not have | traceability | `manual-testing-playbook.md:40` | \"41 `NNN-*.md`\" vs 50 differently named files; same doc says 50 | Readers cannot reconcile the note with the tree | Replace the note with the live 50-file inventory or delete it | Active | traceability | Root playbook in area | playbook §1; inventory test |\n| `iter4-P2-playbook-persistence-path` | P2 | The playbook's persistence contract names a folder the skill does not have | traceability | `manual-testing-playbook.md:30` | No `benchmark/` under the skill root; template names the skill's own folder | A scenario cannot be marked complete as written | Point at a real path or create the folder through the renderer | Active | traceability | Root playbook and skill tree | playbook §2; operator evidence |\n| `iter4-P2-tests-readme-description` | P2 | `runtime/tests/README.md` calls the playbook inventory test a routing-fixture test | maintainability | `runtime/tests/README.md:154` | Test checks playbook rows and file inventory only | A maintainer adds the wrong artifact | Describe the test's actual checks | Active | maintainability | Table and test in area | tests README |\n| `iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode` | P2 | The scorer README says `--row-id` narrows either mode, but session mode ignores it | traceability | `README.md:112` | Flag parsed then unused; `scoreSession` reads only locator/runtime/json | A silent flag and a wrong usage claim | Say \"summary mode\" or refuse the flag in session mode | Active | documentation-drift | README and CLI in area | README; scorer CLI |\n| `iter5-P2-quoted-path-restore` | P2 | A file name git quotes cannot be restored, so one space stops the arm and leaves the file | correctness | `worktree-restore.mjs:54` | `git status --porcelain` prints `?? \"a b.txt\"`; no quote decoding; `rmSync` targets the quoted string | The leftover blocks the next arm until a human deletes it | Parse porcelain quoting (or use `-z`) before restoring | Active | correctness | Restore helper and caller | restore; next arm's dirty guard |\n| `iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report` | P2 | The scorer header promises an ordered read/write report the CLI does not print | maintainability | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:5` | Both modes print counts; the ordered stream is internal only | A maintainer searches for an output that does not exist | Narrow the header to the counts the CLI prints | Active | maintainability | Scorer in area | module header |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\nThere are no P0 or P1 workstreams. The P2 advisories group by file for a single small change:\n\n1. **Behaviour harness correctness** (4 items): `run-command-behaviour.mjs` arm derivation and fixture recording; `command-offer.mjs` log-path trust; `worktree-restore.mjs` porcelain quoting. One worktree, one test each.\n2. **Measurement isolation** (2 items): `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` env restore; `measure-brief-cost.mjs` child-session env. Both are small `try/finally` or env-allowlist edits.\n3. **Packet and playbook docs** (3 items): `spec.md` row 7; `manual-testing-playbook.md:30,40`; `runtime/tests/README.md:154`. Documentation-only.\n4. **Scorer docs** (1 item): `README.md:112` and the scorer header. Documentation-only.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- Add a sentence to the parent phase map row 7 naming the final behaviour arm and the operator instruction that defers T020/T046 and AC-004/005/007.\n- Decide the advisor skill's result-persistence path: create `benchmark/reports/` under the skill or point the playbook at an existing location.\n- Replace the playbook's \"41 `NNN-*.md`\" coverage note with the live 50-file inventory (or delete the historical note).\n- Correct the tests README's description of `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts`.\n- Correct the scorer README's `--row-id` sentence to name summary mode, and narrow the module header.\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- [ ] T1: `run-command-behaviour.mjs` derives the arm from a g2 row id when `--set` is absent; test with `--row-id g2-deep-review-typed`.\n- [ ] T2: record the resolved fixture path on each g2 run line and use it in `--backfill`.\n- [ ] T3: snapshot and restore `process.env` in `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`; test an in-process second scoring call.\n- [ ] T4: strip `AI_SESSION_CHILD` in `measure-brief-cost.mjs` and say so in its README line.\n- [ ] T5: require the backfill's log directory to equal the audited checkout (or refuse a path outside it).\n- [ ] T6: parse porcelain quoting in `statusSnapshot` (or use `git status -z`); add a quoted-name restore test.\n- [ ] T7: the three doc edits and the scorer header, with the inventory test extended to check the coverage note.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n### Core Protocols\n\n- `spec_code`: **pass**. Five pinned routing numbers re-derive from the committed baseline: typed recall 24/44, typed combined reach 44/44, plain tune combined 23/45, false offers 0/35, holdout plain recall 1/44. The command baseline's pinned `capturedAt` (2026-10-11) equals the scorer-eval baseline's, and `capturedAtSha` is an ancestor of HEAD.\n- `checklist_evidence`: **partial**. The parent packet has no checklist; phase 007's T020/T046 and AC-004/005/007 remain open per `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md:141`, and the parent map does not say why (finding 1).\n\n### Overlay Protocols\n\n- `skill_agent`: **notApplicable**. No agent definition owns the accuracy-runner area.\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: **partial**. The six runtime argv tables, the seven-runtime bench matrix and the per-runtime runner branches were read; live per-runtime proof remains phase 007's evidence and is not claimed here.\n- `feature_catalog_code`: **pass**. `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` links NC-001/004/005 and its command semantics match the area.\n- `playbook_capability`: **partial**. NC-011's expected signals and triage symbols hold after the pass-one attach fix; the root playbook's inventory and persistence statements do not.\n\n`AC_COVERAGE`: **exempt**. The packet has no `checklist.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md` or `implementation-summary.md` at the parent level, so the lifecycle predicate is inactive.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- **`run` commands that write.** `/doctor:deep-loop` and `/doctor:speckit` are `run` + `add-only`; whether that is intended belongs to a decision, not this area.\n- **dsh install path.** `/doctor:install` cannot link a dsh runtime; adding a row is a feature decision.\n- **Live per-runtime proof.** Phase 007's final behaviour arm after the merge remains the evidence path; this review could not run a live arm because the worktree is dirty from four concurrent lineages.\n- **Coverage graph.** Unavailable for this lineage; a graph-backed STOP is future work.\n- **`iter3-P2-backfill-log-code-execution` severity.** It is P2 because it needs an untrusted log; if the harness starts accepting logs from other machines by default, it should be revisited as P1.\n\n---\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\n- Saturated directions: none. Remaining frontier: none.\n- Selected review directions per iteration: fix replay, changed-code correctness, security boundaries, traceability and pinned numbers, maintainability of the restore and scorer contracts, stabilization, adjudication.\n- This map records breadth only and changes no verdict.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Search Ledger\n\n- `searchCoverage` (latest iteration): required `severity_inflation`, `duplicate_finding`, `stale_finding`; covered all three; graph mode `graphless_fallback`.\n- `candidateCoverage`: 28 bug classes covered across the seven iterations; `searchDebt` empty; `ruledOutCandidates` 20; `cleanSearchProof` 20.\n- No search debt. Graphless fallback was used throughout: direct reads, exact searches, producer/consumer traces, negative-test inspection and corpus count tallies.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence\n\n- Total iterations: 7; `maxIterations=7` reached; `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\n- `newFindingsRatio` by iteration: 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 0.00, 0.00.\n- The graph prerequisite was unavailable, so no legal graph-backed STOP was claimed. Release readiness: `in-progress`.\n- Dimension coverage: correctness (1-2), security (3), traceability (4), maintainability (5), stabilization (6), adjudication (7).\n\n### Coverage\n\n- 31 area files read at least once; 13 changed-since-pass-one files read at their changed regions.\n- Tests observed: `command-behaviour-guards` + `command-offer` (28 passed), `command-transcript-score` (60 passed), `command-behaviour-guards` + `worktree-restore` (10 passed).\n- Holdout: 44 in-corpus holdout ids and 66 sealed holdout rows; no prompt text printed; 0 holdout ids in any published baseline map.\n\n### Ruled-out Claims\n\n- `offerReached` code wrong (the packet pins the rule; the README was fixed).\n- README code-file count drift (14 code files; 21 entries listed).\n- Bench matrix incomplete (seven runtimes).\n- g2 label grammar drift (`startedLabel` reads `G2_ROWS`).\n- Parse-offer trailing word reach, restore staged-file gap, rename one-sided restore, legacy parity comment contradiction, corpus/fixture drift, holdout leak through fixtures.\n\n### Cross-Reference Appendix\n\n**Core Protocols**\n- `spec_code`: pass (five floors + pinned clock).\n- `checklist_evidence`: partial (phase 007 open rows; no parent checklist).\n\n**Overlay Protocols**\n- `skill_agent`: notApplicable.\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: partial (read evidence; live proof phase 007).\n- `feature_catalog_code`: pass.\n- `playbook_capability`: partial (NC-011 holds; root playbook advisories).\n\n### Sources Reviewed\n\n- The 31 `accuracy-runner` files of `review/review-scope-2.txt`, the CLI and test files they import, the shared `system-skill-advisor/README.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md`, the manual-testing-playbook root and NC-011 chapter, and `spec.md`/`007/tasks.md` as traceability context.\n\n### Lineage Note\n\nThe reducer-owned registry carries the twelve findings but leaves `findingClass` empty (the same shape as pass one). The class column above comes from the iteration records, which carry `findingClass` per finding.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build — accuracy-runner-2 (pass two)\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: lineage=accuracy-runner-2; sessionId=fanout-accuracy-runner-2-1794570021136-noekp0; generation=1; lineageMode=new; stopReason=maxIterationsReached -->\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Overall verdict:** PASS\\n- **hasAdvisories:** true\\n- **Active findings:** P0 = 0, P1 = 0, P2 = 12\\n- **Review scope:** the pass-two `accuracy-runner` area of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`: the routing-accuracy harness, prompt corpora and committed baselines, transcript and offer tests, cost measurements, legacy fidelity tests and the manual-testing playbook. 31 area files plus the shared docs that describe them; 13 area files changed since pass one and 18 unchanged.\\n- **Operator review focus:** Code review of command surfacing, PASS TWO. First read the full instructions in the pass-two instructions file and follow them: for each pass-one finding in the accuracy-runner area, re-read the code and say whether the fix holds; review every file marked yes (changed since pass one) line by line for a defect the fix introduced; then look for new defects. Scope file lists area, path and changed-since-pass-one. Check behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; safety of offering a mutating command; holdout hygiene, so no tune, fix or report path reads or leaks holdout rows; docs that disagree with code. Never read or print holdout prompt text (split holdout in command-prompts.jsonl, or holdout-prompts.jsonl): counts only. Change no code, write only inside the lineage folder.\\n- **Headline:** eight of the nine pass-one findings this lineage raised hold; the ninth (the parent phase map) is only half fixed and is reported again. The changed code introduced no new P0 or P1. The pass-two findings are ten P2s about measurement attribution, process isolation, a run-log trust boundary, a restore edge, and four docs that disagree with the tree or the code.\\n- **Loop state:** `maxIterations=7` reached; the coverage graph was unavailable, so a legal graph-backed STOP was not claimable. Release readiness is `in-progress`, not `converged`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\n`/speckit:plan` is **not required** for this lineage: there is no active P0, no active P1 and no failed binary gate. The twelve P2s are advisories for the remediation owner.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": false,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": true,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": 12,\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\\"Close or annotate phase 007 in the parent phase map\\\", \\\"Correct the manual-testing-playbook inventory note, persistence path and tests-README description\\\"],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\\"Fix the four harness advisories in one small group\\\", \\\"Add the missing tests named in the registry\\\"],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"measurement-correctness\\\", \\\"process-isolation\\\", \\\"security\\\", \\\"traceability\\\", \\\"maintainability\\\", \\\"correctness\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\\"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy\\\", \\\"runtime/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs\\\", \\\"manual-testing-playbook\\\", \\\"runtime/tests/README.md\\\", \\\"spec.md\\\"],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Sev | Title | Dimension | File:line | Evidence | Impact | Fix recommendation | Disposition | Finding class | Scope proof | Affected surfaces |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence` | P2 | The pass-one phase-map finding is only half fixed: the reason lives in the phase child, not in the map the finding named | traceability | `spec.md:122` | Row 7 `In Progress` beside completed 008 and 010-013; reason only at `007/tasks.md:141` | A parent-map reader cannot tell an intentional deferral from a skipped phase | Add one sentence to row 7 or a note under the map naming the final behaviour arm | Active | traceability | Packet spec is the review target; the item was raised by this lineage | `spec.md`; `007/tasks.md:141` |\\n| `iter2-P2-g2-row-id-arm-mislabel` | P2 | A started-command row selected by `--row-id` is logged under the `pre` arm | correctness | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:974` | `armFor` keys only on `options.set`; `assertRunnable` accepts g2 ids | A 15-minute g2 turn joins the pre arm and skews the comparison | Derive the arm from the row id when the set is absent, or refuse `--row-id` g2 ids without `--arm` | Active | measurement-correctness | Runner and scorer in scope | run line; scorer bucketing |\\n| `iter2-P2-backfill-fixture-mismatch` | P2 | `--backfill` replays a g2 row with the default fixture even when the run used a custom one | correctness | `run-command-behaviour.mjs:1214` | Run uses `options.fixture`; backfill re-derives `g2-fixture` from its own log path | The replayed offer describes a prompt the turn never ran | Record the fixture path on the run line or add `--fixture` to the backfill | Active | measurement-correctness | Runner and backfill in scope | run log; `command-offer.mjs` backfill |\\n| `iter2-P2-capture-env-not-restored` | P2 | The capture leaves its environment projection installed after it returns | correctness | `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:361` | Five env vars written and four deleted; `finally` restores only `Date` and removes the temp dir | A second in-process score inherits a deleted DB dir and the fixture regime | Snapshot and restore `process.env` in the `finally` | Active | process-isolation | Capture module and its in-process caller | capture; slice test |\\n| `iter2-P2-cost-script-child-brief` | P2 | `measure-brief-cost.mjs` measures the child-session brief from a dispatched worker | correctness | `measure-brief-cost.mjs:167` | Hook env spreads `process.env`; renderer reads `AI_SESSION_CHILD` | The reported cost is the child brief, not the user brief | Strip `AI_SESSION_CHILD` (and state it) before spawning the hook | Active | measurement-correctness | Cost script and renderer branch | cost figures |\\n| `iter3-P2-backfill-log-code-execution` | P2 | `--backfill` executes the hook and advisor CLI from the directory a log line names | security | `command-offer.mjs:333` | `checkoutDir` comes from `locator.projectDir`; `warmCheckout` and `replayOffer` spawn from it | A crafted log selects the JavaScript the backfill runs | Require the log's directory to equal the audited checkout, or refuse a path outside the repo | Active | security | Backfill and its caller | backfill path |\\n| `iter4-P2-playbook-inventory-note` | P2 | The playbook's coverage note names a file convention and count the tree does not have | traceability | `manual-testing-playbook.md:40` | \\\"41 `NNN-*.md`\\\" vs 50 differently named files; same doc says 50 | Readers cannot reconcile the note with the tree | Replace the note with the live 50-file inventory or delete it | Active | traceability | Root playbook in area | playbook §1; inventory test |\\n| `iter4-P2-playbook-persistence-path` | P2 | The playbook's persistence contract names a folder the skill does not have | traceability | `manual-testing-playbook.md:30` | No `benchmark/` under the skill root; template names the skill's own folder | A scenario cannot be marked complete as written | Point at a real path or create the folder through the renderer | Active | traceability | Root playbook and skill tree | playbook §2; operator evidence |\\n| `iter4-P2-tests-readme-description` | P2 | `runtime/tests/README.md` calls the playbook inventory test a routing-fixture test | maintainability | `runtime/tests/README.md:154` | Test checks playbook rows and file inventory only | A maintainer adds the wrong artifact | Describe the test's actual checks | Active | maintainability | Table and test in area | tests README |\\n| `iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode` | P2 | The scorer README says `--row-id` narrows either mode, but session mode ignores it | traceability | `README.md:112` | Flag parsed then unused; `scoreSession` reads only locator/runtime/json | A silent flag and a wrong usage claim | Say \\\"summary mode\\\" or refuse the flag in session mode | Active | documentation-drift | README and CLI in area | README; scorer CLI |\\n| `iter5-P2-quoted-path-restore` | P2 | A file name git quotes cannot be restored, so one space stops the arm and leaves the file | correctness | `worktree-restore.mjs:54` | `git status --porcelain` prints `?? \\\"a b.txt\\\"`; no quote decoding; `rmSync` targets the quoted string | The leftover blocks the next arm until a human deletes it | Parse porcelain quoting (or use `-z`) before restoring | Active | correctness | Restore helper and caller | restore; next arm's dirty guard |\\n| `iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report` | P2 | The scorer header promises an ordered read/write report the CLI does not print | maintainability | `score-command-transcripts.mjs:5` | Both modes print counts; the ordered stream is internal only | A maintainer searches for an output that does not exist | Narrow the header to the counts the CLI prints | Active | maintainability | Scorer in area | module header |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\nThere are no P0 or P1 workstreams. The P2 advisories group by file for a single small change:\\n\\n1. **Behaviour harness correctness** (4 items): `run-command-behaviour.mjs` arm derivation and fixture recording; `command-offer.mjs` log-path trust; `worktree-restore.mjs` porcelain quoting. One worktree, one test each.\\n2. **Measurement isolation** (2 items): `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` env restore; `measure-brief-cost.mjs` child-session env. Both are small `try/finally` or env-allowlist edits.\\n3. **Packet and playbook docs** (3 items): `spec.md` row 7; `manual-testing-playbook.md:30,40`; `runtime/tests/README.md:154`. Documentation-only.\\n4. **Scorer docs** (1 item): `README.md:112` and the scorer header. Documentation-only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- Add a sentence to the parent phase map row 7 naming the final behaviour arm and the operator instruction that defers T020/T046 and AC-004/005/007.\\n- Decide the advisor skill's result-persistence path: create `benchmark/reports/` under the skill or point the playbook at an existing location.\\n- Replace the playbook's \\\"41 `NNN-*.md`\\\" coverage note with the live 50-file inventory (or delete the historical note).\\n- Correct the tests README's description of `manual-testing-playbook.vitest.ts`.\\n- Correct the scorer README's `--row-id` sentence to name summary mode, and narrow the module header.\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- [ ] T1: `run-command-behaviour.mjs` derives the arm from a g2 row id when `--set` is absent; test with `--row-id g2-deep-review-typed`.\\n- [ ] T2: record the resolved fixture path on each g2 run line and use it in `--backfill`.\\n- [ ] T3: snapshot and restore `process.env` in `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`; test an in-process second scoring call.\\n- [ ] T4: strip `AI_SESSION_CHILD` in `measure-brief-cost.mjs` and say so in its README line.\\n- [ ] T5: require the backfill's log directory to equal the audited checkout (or refuse a path outside it).\\n- [ ] T6: parse porcelain quoting in `statusSnapshot` (or use `git status -z`); add a quoted-name restore test.\\n- [ ] T7: the three doc edits and the scorer header, with the inventory test extended to check the coverage note.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n### Core Protocols\\n\\n- `spec_code`: **pass**. Five pinned routing numbers re-derive from the committed baseline: typed recall 24/44, typed combined reach 44/44, plain tune combined 23/45, false offers 0/35, holdout plain recall 1/44. The command baseline's pinned `capturedAt` (2026-10-11) equals the scorer-eval baseline's, and `capturedAtSha` is an ancestor of HEAD.\\n- `checklist_evidence`: **partial**. The parent packet has no checklist; phase 007's T020/T046 and AC-004/005/007 remain open per `007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/tasks.md:141`, and the parent map does not say why (finding 1).\\n\\n### Overlay Protocols\\n\\n- `skill_agent`: **notApplicable**. No agent definition owns the accuracy-runner area.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: **partial**. The six runtime argv tables, the seven-runtime bench matrix and the per-runtime runner branches were read; live per-runtime proof remains phase 007's evidence and is not claimed here.\\n- `feature_catalog_code`: **pass**. `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` links NC-001/004/005 and its command semantics match the area.\\n- `playbook_capability`: **partial**. NC-011's expected signals and triage symbols hold after the pass-one attach fix; the root playbook's inventory and persistence statements do not.\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE`: **exempt**. The packet has no `checklist.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md` or `implementation-summary.md` at the parent level, so the lifecycle predicate is inactive.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- **`run` commands that write.** `/doctor:deep-loop` and `/doctor:speckit` are `run` + `add-only`; whether that is intended belongs to a decision, not this area.\\n- **dsh install path.** `/doctor:install` cannot link a dsh runtime; adding a row is a feature decision.\\n- **Live per-runtime proof.** Phase 007's final behaviour arm after the merge remains the evidence path; this review could not run a live arm because the worktree is dirty from four concurrent lineages.\\n- **Coverage graph.** Unavailable for this lineage; a graph-backed STOP is future work.\\n- **`iter3-P2-backfill-log-code-execution` severity.** It is P2 because it needs an untrusted log; if the harness starts accepting logs from other machines by default, it should be revisited as P1.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0. Failed pivots: 0. Audited overrides: 0.\\n- Saturated directions: none. Remaining frontier: none.\\n- Selected review directions per iteration: fix replay, changed-code correctness, security boundaries, traceability and pinned numbers, maintainability of the restore and scorer contracts, stabilization, adjudication.\\n- This map records breadth only and changes no verdict.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Search Ledger\\n\\n- `searchCoverage` (latest iteration): required `severity_inflation`, `duplicate_finding`, `stale_finding`; covered all three; graph mode `graphless_fallback`.\\n- `candidateCoverage`: 28 bug classes covered across the seven iterations; `searchDebt` empty; `ruledOutCandidates` 20; `cleanSearchProof` 20.\\n- No search debt. Graphless fallback was used throughout: direct reads, exact searches, producer/consumer traces, negative-test inspection and corpus count tallies.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence\\n\\n- Total iterations: 7; `maxIterations=7` reached; `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`.\\n- `newFindingsRatio` by iteration: 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 0.00, 0.00.\\n- The graph prerequisite was unavailable, so no legal graph-backed STOP was claimed. Release readiness: `in-progress`.\\n- Dimension coverage: correctness (1-2), security (3), traceability (4), maintainability (5), stabilization (6), adjudication (7).\\n\\n### Coverage\\n\\n- 31 area files read at least once; 13 changed-since-pass-one files read at their changed regions.\\n- Tests observed: `command-behaviour-guards` + `command-offer` (28 passed), `command-transcript-score` (60 passed), `command-behaviour-guards` + `worktree-restore` (10 passed).\\n- Holdout: 44 in-corpus holdout ids and 66 sealed holdout rows; no prompt text printed; 0 holdout ids in any published baseline map.\\n\\n### Ruled-out Claims\\n\\n- `offerReached` code wrong (the packet pins the rule; the README was fixed).\\n- README code-file count drift (14 code files; 21 entries listed).\\n- Bench matrix incomplete (seven runtimes).\\n- g2 label grammar drift (`startedLabel` reads `G2_ROWS`).\\n- Parse-offer trailing word reach, restore staged-file gap, rename one-sided restore, legacy parity comment contradiction, corpus/fixture drift, holdout leak through fixtures.\\n\\n### Cross-Reference Appendix\\n\\n**Core Protocols**\\n- `spec_code`: pass (five floors + pinned clock).\\n- `checklist_evidence`: partial (phase 007 open rows; no parent checklist).\\n\\n**Overlay Protocols**\\n- `skill_agent`: notApplicable.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime`: partial (read evidence; live proof phase 007).\\n- `feature_catalog_code`: pass.\\n- `playbook_capability`: partial (NC-011 holds; root playbook advisories).\\n\\n### Sources Reviewed\\n\\n- The 31 `accuracy-runner` files of `review/review-scope-2.txt`, the CLI and test files they import, the shared `system-skill-advisor/README.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md`, the manual-testing-playbook root and NC-011 chapter, and `spec.md`/`007/tasks.md` as traceability context.\\n\\n### Lineage Note\\n\\nThe reducer-owned registry carries the twelve findings but leaves `findingClass` empty (the same shape as pass one). The class column above comes from the iteration records, which carry `findingClass` per finding.\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-2/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794572377968,"end":1794572417195}}}}
